t.clj\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"line_offset\\\\\\\":1210,\\\\\\\"n_lines\\\\\\\":90}\\\"}},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"function\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"tool_Dhy3TdSucP9fqhc6riFDoiLw\\\",\\\"function\\\":{\\\"name\\\":\\\"Read\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":\\\"{\\\\\\\"path\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"docs/design/yang.antlr.md\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"line_offset\\\\\\\":1940,\\\\\\\"n_lines\\\\\\\":70}\\\"}},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"function\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"tool_rPdsl4iKkDlp7W5jwOBId93S\\\",\\\"function\\\":{\\\"name\\\":\\\"Read\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":\\\"{\\\\\\\"path\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"line_offset\\\\\\\":2470,\\\\\\\"n_lines\\\\\\\":135}\\\"}}]}\\n{\\\"role\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool_call_id\\\":\\\"tool_Dhy3TdSucP9fqhc6riFDoiLw\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"1940\\\\toptimization belongs to an attached optimizer and must preserve these\\\\n1941\\\\tobservations and runtime rebinding of the consumer. List, set, and dict\\\\n1942\\\\tcomprehensions stay eager. `yield` at module or class level, or inside\\\\n1943\\\\tany comprehension or generator expression, is a syntax diagnostic.\\\\n1944\\\\t\\\\n1945\\\\t`py/iter-at` keeps its index signature as an internal compatibility\\\\n1946\\\\tinterface, not the public iterator protocol (ruling 5). A stateful\\\\n1947\\\\titerator advances once per call and ignores the index; iterable\\\\n1948\\\\tacquisition happens once per loop; `iter(iterator)` preserves identity;\\\\n1949\\\\texhaustion handling covers only the advancement, never the loop body.\\\\n1950\\\\tThe loop counter must not overflow or round under long consumption: it\\\\n1951\\\\tuses exact increment once C3 lands, without narrowing generator\\\\n1952\\\\tpayloads.\\\\n1953\\\\t\\\\n1954\\\\tUser-defined iterator classes are part of C2, in S5 (ruling 8).\\\\n1955\\\\tImplicit `__iter__` and `__next__` lookup uses the type's special-method\\\\n1956\\\\tpath, since ordinary `py/getattr` prefers instance attributes; it\\\\n1957\\\\tvalidates the returned iterator and catches `StopIteration` only around\\\\n1958\\\\tadvancement. Termination values are preserved for delegation, other\\\\n1959\\\\texceptions propagate, and optional `send`, `throw`, and `close` are\\\\n1960\\\\tforwarded per PEP 380.\\\\n1961\\\\t\\\\n1962\\\\tNo generator flag is persisted on function specs (ruling 9). Generator\\\\n1963\\\\tstatus is decided during scope-aware lowering, excluding nested function\\\\n1964\\\\tbodies and including unreachable `yield` and `yield from`, and is\\\\n1965\\\\tencoded in ordinary code. Future introspection, such as\\\\n1966\\\\t`inspect.isgeneratorfunction`, derives status from the scoped\\\\n1967\\\\tgenerator-construction pattern; a query for direct applications of\\\\n1968\\\\t`py/yield` alone is insufficient, because a body using only `yield from`\\\\n1969\\\\tneed not apply it.\\\\n1970\\\\t\\\\n1971\\\\tHeap, identity, and wire:\\\\n1972\\\\t\\\\n1973\\\\t- Tracing needs no VM change: cell content is traced as data and a\\\\n1974\\\\t  continuation is walked through its payload.\\\\n1975\\\\t- An unreachable generator is reclaimed without an implicit `close()`\\\\n1976\\\\t  (ruling 6). Python specifies a `close()` on generator finalization, so\\\\n1977\\\\t  this is an explicit finalization restriction of the support profile,\\\\n1978\\\\t  not conformance. The landed collector has no finalizers; explicit\\\\n1979\\\\t  `close()` stays supported. Pinning roots the generator cell and traces\\\\n1980\\\\t  its current content, not every historical continuation.\\\\n1981\\\\t- `%capture` is undelimited, so `:resume` holds the frames of the first\\\\n1982\\\\t  `next()` call beneath the generator's own (stale base). This fixed\\\\n1983\\\\t  retention is accepted for C2; growth per yield is rejected (ruling 7).\\\\n1984\\\\t  Delimited capture is a separate VM question.\\\\n1985\\\\t- A suspended generator does not migrate: cells refuse lift and\\\\n1986\\\\t  continuations refuse as `:non-canonicalizable`. Once heap lift and a\\\\n1987\\\\t  continuation encoding land, generators migrate with no\\\\n1988\\\\t  generator-specific wire form; until then the refusal stays.\\\\n1989\\\\t- `is` is `=` on the ref, `iter(g) is g`, and a generator is a dict key\\\\n1990\\\\t  by ref through the non-numeric arm of `py/key`. `py/snapshot-obj`\\\\n1991\\\\t  renders `{:py/generator name}`, diagnostic data, never a resumable\\\\n1992\\\\t  wire form. The prelude compares only `:state` keywords, never\\\\n1993\\\\t  generator contents, since continuation equality and hash are\\\\n1994\\\\t  structural.\\\\n1995\\\\t- The canonical tree changes only by new prelude functions: `yield` is\\\\n1996\\\\t  an `:application` of `py/yield`, and `%capture` stays inside the\\\\n1997\\\\t  prelude. The prelude grows, so every bundled unit's address changes,\\\\n1998\\\\t  a prelude-profile bump under section 11.\\\\n1999\\\\t\\\\n2000\\\\tFor safepoints, generator switches happen only at applications of\\\\n2001\\\\t`py/gen-switch`, `py/yield-raw`, and `py/yield-from`, which an attached\\\\n2002\\\\tinserter can find by query; `sys.settrace` sees nothing in C2. Future\\\\n2003\\\\tper-thread dynamic state (the frame-record stack, the recursion counter,\\\\n2004\\\\t`exc_info`) joins `:ctx` and swaps with the handler stack.\\\\n2005\\\\t\\\\n2006\\\\t```text\\\\n2007\\\\t+--------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+\\\\n2008\\\\t| Slice  | Scope                                                               |\\\\n2009\\\\t+========+=====================================================================+\\\"}\\n{\\\"role\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool_call_id\\\":\\\"tool_rPdsl4iKkDlp7W5jwOBId93S\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"2470\\\\t    (let [id (:id x)\\\\n2471\\\\t          entry (get heap id)]\\\\n2472\\\\t      (when (and (some? entry) (= (:seal x) (:seal entry))) id))))\\\\n2473\\\\t\\\\n2474\\\\t\\\\n2475\\\\t(defn- moded\\\\n2476\\\\t  \\\\\\\"`work` with each of `xs` pushed in `mode`, `:kernel` or `:data`.\\\\\\\"\\\\n2477\\\\t  [work mode xs]\\\\n2478\\\\t  (into work (map (fn [x] [mode x])) xs))\\\\n2479\\\\t\\\\n2480\\\\t\\\\n2481\\\\t(defn- trace\\\\n2482\\\\t  \\\\\\\"`found` plus the ids of `heap` reachable from `roots`, a map\\\\n2483\\\\t   `{:kernel [...] :data [...]}` of root values by mode. Two modes keep\\\\n2484\\\\t   guest data from being read as kernel shapes (gemini reclamation gate,\\\\n2485\\\\t   concern 1):\\\\n2486\\\\t\\\\n2487\\\\t   - `:kernel`, a value in a kernel position (a kernel root, an engine\\\\n2488\\\\t     table entry, a closure or continuation payload, or a kernel child of\\\\n2489\\\\t     one): the kernel's `gc-children` may interpret it, and answers which\\\\n2490\\\\t     of its children are kernel positions and which are values. A value\\\\n2491\\\\t     it does not recognize is walked whole, as data.\\\\n2492\\\\t   - `:data`, a value position (an environment value, an operand, a\\\\n2493\\\\t     register, a cell's content): every map is walked whole, never\\\\n2494\\\\t     pruned, so a guest map shaped like a frame cannot hide a cell ref.\\\\n2495\\\\t     Only a closure or continuation, a host type no guest can forge,\\\\n2496\\\\t     re-enters `:kernel` mode through its payload.\\\\n2497\\\\t\\\\n2498\\\\t   Scalars hold nothing. With `follow?` a newly found id's content is\\\\n2499\\\\t   traced too, as data (marking); without, only the refs met directly\\\\n2500\\\\t   (pinning). Each value is visited once per mode, so shared environments\\\\n2501\\\\t   cost one walk and a cell holding its own ref terminates. The worklist\\\\n2502\\\\t   is explicit: a deep continuation chain does not grow the host stack.\\\\\\\"\\\\n2503\\\\t  [vm heap roots found follow?]\\\\n2504\\\\t  (let [children-of (if (satisfies? module/IModuleKernel vm)\\\\n2505\\\\t                      #(module/gc-children vm %)\\\\n2506\\\\t                      (constantly nil))]\\\\n2507\\\\t    (loop [work (-> ()\\\\n2508\\\\t                    (moded :kernel (:kernel roots))\\\\n2509\\\\t                    (moded :data (:data roots)))\\\\n2510\\\\t           seen #{}\\\\n2511\\\\t           found found]\\\\n2512\\\\t      (if (empty? work)\\\\n2513\\\\t        found\\\\n2514\\\\t        (let [[mode x :as entry] (peek work)\\\\n2515\\\\t              work (pop work)]\\\\n2516\\\\t          (if (or (scalar? x) (contains? seen entry))\\\\n2517\\\\t            (recur work seen found)\\\\n2518\\\\t            (let [id (when (map? x) (heap-ref-id heap x))\\\\n2519\\\\t                  new-id? (and (some? id) (not (contains? found id)))\\\\n2520\\\\t                  children (when (and (= :kernel mode)\\\\n2521\\\\t                                      (not (values/host-typed? x)))\\\\n2522\\\\t                             (children-of x))\\\\n2523\\\\t                  work (cond-> work\\\\n2524\\\\t                         (and new-id? follow?)\\\\n2525\\\\t                         (conj [:data (:value (get heap id))])\\\\n2526\\\\t                         (values/host-typed? x)\\\\n2527\\\\t                         (conj [:kernel (values/payload x)])\\\\n2528\\\\t                         (some? children)\\\\n2529\\\\t                         (-> (moded :kernel (:kernel children))\\\\n2530\\\\t                             (moded :data (:values children)))\\\\n2531\\\\t                         (and (nil? children) (map? x))\\\\n2532\\\\t                         (-> (moded :data (keys x))\\\\n2533\\\\t                             (moded :data (vals x)))\\\\n2534\\\\t                         (and (nil? children) (not (map? x)) (coll? x))\\\\n2535\\\\t                         (moded :data x))]\\\\n2536\\\\t              (recur work\\\\n2537\\\\t                     (conj seen entry)\\\\n2538\\\\t                     (if new-id? (conj found id) found)))))))))\\\\n2539\\\\t\\\\n2540\\\\t\\\\n2541\\\\t(defn- gc-roots\\\\n2542\\\\t  \\\\\\\"Every root of `vm` (design Q1), by mode: the kernel's registers as it\\\\n2543\\\\t   classifies them (`module/gc-roots`), each entry of `:parked`,\\\\n2544\\\\t   `:wait-set` and `:ready-queue` as a kernel position, the store and\\\\n2545\\\\t   every module store as values, then `extra` as values. Code, images,\\\\n2546\\\\t   the registry, primitives, `:callable-effects`, telemetry and\\\\n2547\\\\t   `:resources` are not roots: a literal can never be an authentic ref,\\\\n2548\\\\t   and a value inside a stream is the medium's (hence pinning).\\\\\\\"\\\\n2549\\\\t  [vm extra]\\\\n2550\\\\t  (let [kernel (when (satisfies? module/IModuleKernel vm)\\\\n2551\\\\t                 (module/gc-roots vm))]\\\\n2552\\\\t    {:kernel (-> (vec (:kernel kernel))\\\\n2553\\\\t                 (into (vals (:parked vm)))\\\\n2554\\\\t                 (into (:wait-set vm))\\\\n2555\\\\t                 (into (:ready-queue vm))),\\\\n2556\\\\t     :data (-> [(:store vm) (:module-stores vm)]\\\\n2557\\\\t               (into (:values kernel))\\\\n2558\\\\t               (into extra))}))\\\\n2559\\\\t\\\\n2560\\\\t\\\\n2561\\\\t(defn- mark\\\\n2562\\\\t  \\\\\\\"The ids of `heap` live from `roots` and from the `pinned` ids: a pinned\\\\n2563\\\\t   cell is a root, so its content is traced too, as data.\\\\\\\"\\\\n2564\\\\t  [vm heap roots pinned]\\\\n2565\\\\t  (let [pins (filterv #(contains? heap %) pinned)]\\\\n2566\\\\t    (trace vm\\\\n2567\\\\t           heap\\\\n2568\\\\t           (update roots :data into (map #(:value (get heap %))) pins)\\\\n2569\\\\t           (set pins)\\\\n2570\\\\t           true)))\\\\n2571\\\\t\\\\n2572\\\\t\\\\n2573\\\\t(defn- sweep\\\\n2574\\\\t  \\\\\\\"`heap` without each id of the cycle's `snapshot` that `marked` lacks.\\\\n2575\\\\t   An id allocated after the snapshot is not in it, so it is spared.\\\\\\\"\\\\n2576\\\\t  [heap snapshot marked]\\\\n2577\\\\t  (reduce-kv (fn [h id _] (if (contains? marked id) h (dissoc h id)))\\\\n2578\\\\t             heap\\\\n2579\\\\t             snapshot))\\\\n2580\\\\t\\\\n2581\\\\t\\\\n2582\\\\t(defn- gc-of\\\\n2583\\\\t  [state]\\\\n2584\\\\t  (or (:gc state) (vm/fresh-gc nil)))\\\\n2585\\\\t\\\\n2586\\\\t\\\\n2587\\\\t(defn collect\\\\n2588\\\\t  \\\\\\\"`vm` after one stop-the-world collection of its `:heap`, with `extra`\\\\n2589\\\\t   traced as additional roots. The allocation count restarts and the\\\\n2590\\\\t   threshold becomes `max(base, 2 x live)`, so the total work stays linear\\\\n2591\\\\t   in allocations. Pure: the same state always collects to the same heap.\\\\\\\"\\\\n2592\\\\t  ([vm] (collect vm nil))\\\\n2593\\\\t  ([vm extra]\\\\n2594\\\\t   (let [gc (gc-of vm)\\\\n2595\\\\t         snapshot (:heap vm)\\\\n2596\\\\t         marked (mark vm snapshot (gc-roots vm extra) (:pinned gc))\\\\n2597\\\\t         heap (sweep (:heap vm) snapshot marked)]\\\\n2598\\\\t     (assoc vm\\\\n2599\\\\t            :heap heap\\\\n2600\\\\t            :gc (assoc gc\\\\n2601\\\\t                       :since 0\\\\n2602\\\\t                       :threshold (max (:base gc) (* 2 (count heap))))))))\\\\n2603\\\\t\\\\n2604\\\\t\\\"}\\n{\\\"role\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool_call_id\\\":\\\"tool_lT20OSARruxXAukgGgd9EAUR\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"1210\\\\t            generator's :resume grows per item\\\\\\\"\\\\n1211\\\\t    (doseq [k [:ast-walker :semantic :stack :register]]\\\\n1212\\\\t      (testing (str k)\\\\n1213\\\\t        (is (= (suspended-resume-sizes k 2 (counter-source 10 true))\\\\n1214\\\\t               (suspended-resume-sizes k 2 (counter-source 1000 true))))))))\\\\n1215\\\\t\\\\n1216\\\\t\\\\n1217\\\\t(defn- deep-size\\\\n1218\\\\t  \\\\\\\"Node count of `x` with continuation and closure payloads followed; a\\\\n1219\\\\t   cell ref counts as itself (its cell is counted once, as a heap entry).\\\\\\\"\\\\n1220\\\\t  [x]\\\\n1221\\\\t  (cond\\\\n1222\\\\t    (values/host-typed? x) (+ 1 (deep-size (values/payload x)))\\\\n1223\\\\t    (map? x) (reduce + 1 (map deep-size (concat (keys x) (vals x))))\\\\n1224\\\\t    (coll? x) (reduce + 1 (map deep-size x))\\\\n1225\\\\t    :else 1))\\\\n1226\\\\t\\\\n1227\\\\t\\\\n1228\\\\t(defn- live-after-collection\\\\n1229\\\\t  \\\\\\\"[live cell count, deep size of all live cell content] once VM `k` ran\\\\n1230\\\\t   `source` and its final state was collected with the suspended\\\\n1231\\\\t   generator named `root` as the only extra root: everything that\\\\n1232\\\\t   generator reaches, continuations followed, not one `:resume` alone.\\\\n1233\\\\t   The module's own globals are garbage once it completes, so without the\\\\n1234\\\\t   root nothing of the program would be live.\\\\\\\"\\\\n1235\\\\t  [k source root]\\\\n1236\\\\t  (let [ast (lower/lower-packet\\\\n1237\\\\t              (parser/parse-source (parser/make-worker) [:u 1] source))\\\\n1238\\\\t        final ((get final-vms k) ast (vm/ast->datoms ast))\\\\n1239\\\\t        roots (into []\\\\n1240\\\\t                    (keep (fn [[id {:keys [value seal]}]]\\\\n1241\\\\t                            (when (and (= :generator (:py/type value))\\\\n1242\\\\t                                       (= :suspended (:state value))\\\\n1243\\\\t                                       (= root (:name value)))\\\\n1244\\\\t                              {:type :cell-ref, :id id, :seal seal})))\\\\n1245\\\\t                    (:heap final))\\\\n1246\\\\t        heap (:heap (engine/collect final roots))]\\\\n1247\\\\t    (is (= 1 (count roots)) (str k \\\\\\\" one suspended \\\\\\\" root))\\\\n1248\\\\t    [(count heap) (reduce + (map (fn [[_ {:keys [value]}]] (deep-size value)) heap))]))\\\\n1249\\\\t\\\\n1250\\\\t\\\\n1251\\\\t(defn- changing-caller-source\\\\n1252\\\\t  \\\\\\\"`n` items through a `yield from` level, resumed alternately by a\\\\n1253\\\\t   function and by a fresh generator dropped after one step.\\\\\\\"\\\\n1254\\\\t  [n]\\\\n1255\\\\t  (lines \\\\\\\"def g():\\\\\\\"\\\\n1256\\\\t         \\\\\\\"    i = 0\\\\\\\"\\\\n1257\\\\t         \\\\\\\"    while True:\\\\\\\"\\\\n1258\\\\t         \\\\\\\"        yield i\\\\\\\"\\\\n1259\\\\t         \\\\\\\"        i += 1\\\\\\\"\\\\n1260\\\\t         \\\\\\\"def h():\\\\\\\"\\\\n1261\\\\t         \\\\\\\"    yield from g()\\\\\\\"\\\\n1262\\\\t         \\\\\\\"it = h()\\\\\\\"\\\\n1263\\\\t         \\\\\\\"def by_function(x):\\\\\\\"\\\\n1264\\\\t         \\\\\\\"    return next(x)\\\\\\\"\\\\n1265\\\\t         \\\\\\\"def by_generator(x):\\\\\\\"\\\\n1266\\\\t         \\\\\\\"    yield next(x)\\\\\\\"\\\\n1267\\\\t         \\\\\\\"k = 0\\\\\\\"\\\\n1268\\\\t         (str \\\\\\\"while k < \\\\\\\" n \\\\\\\":\\\\\\\")\\\\n1269\\\\t         \\\\\\\"    if k % 2 == 0:\\\\\\\"\\\\n1270\\\\t         \\\\\\\"        by_function(it)\\\\\\\"\\\\n1271\\\\t         \\\\\\\"    else:\\\\\\\"\\\\n1272\\\\t         \\\\\\\"        next(by_generator(it))\\\\\\\"\\\\n1273\\\\t         \\\\\\\"    k += 1\\\\\\\"))\\\\n1274\\\\t\\\\n1275\\\\t\\\\n1276\\\\t(deftest ^:slow reachable-heap-is-stable-under-delegation-test\\\\n1277\\\\t  (testing \\\\\\\"after a forced collection, the live heap (cells and their content,\\\\n1278\\\\t            continuations followed) is the same after 10 and after 1000 items\\\\n1279\\\\t            resumed through yield from by changing callers: no retention\\\\n1280\\\\t            grows per item or per caller\\\\\\\"\\\\n1281\\\\t    (doseq [k [:ast-walker :semantic :stack :register]]\\\\n1282\\\\t      (testing (str k)\\\\n1283\\\\t        (is (= (live-after-collection k (changing-caller-source 10) \\\\\\\"h\\\\\\\")\\\\n1284\\\\t               (live-after-collection k (changing-caller-source 1000) \\\\\\\"h\\\\\\\")))))))\\\\n1285\\\\t\\\\n1286\\\\t\\\\n1287\\\\t;; =============================================================================\\\\n1288\\\\t;; S5 acceptance: user-defined iterators, snapshot rendering, dropped generators\\\\n1289\\\\t;; =============================================================================\\\\n1290\\\\t\\\\n1291\\\\t(deftest user-iterator-class-test\\\\n1292\\\\t  (testing \\\\\\\"a class with __iter__ and __next__ drives for, list, next and\\\\n1293\\\\t            unpacking; a shared iterator keeps its position across loops\\\\\\\"\\\\n1294\\\\t    (every-vm= (prints \\\\\\\"[3, 4, 5]\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"done\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"[1, 2, 3]\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"1 2\\\\\\\")\\\\n1295\\\\t               (lines \\\\\\\"class Count:\\\\\\\"\\\\n1296\\\\t                      \\\\\\\"    def __init__(self, n):\\\\\\\"\\\\n1297\\\\t                      \\\\\\\"        self.i = 0\\\\\\\"\\\\n1298\\\\t                      \\\\\\\"        self.n = n\\\\\\\"\\\\n1299\\\\t                      \\\\\\\"    def __iter__(self):\\\\\\\"\\\"}\\n{\\\"role\\\":\\\"assistant\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"## Ruling: **(c), the measurement is wrong—not the assertion**\\\\n\\\\nThe PHP fixture blocks **before module shutdown**. Consequently, `engine/collect` still traces the blocked main activation, its globals, continuation, and temporary/CV state in addition to the supplied generator reference. The `roots` argument contains **extra roots**, not replacement roots (`src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:2541-2558`, `:2587-2597`).\\\\n\\\\nThus 151 versus 5,596 cells measures different module-frame live sets, not growth owned by the suspended generator. There is no evidence here of a generator retention leak.\\\\n\\\\nThe last `$j` is not the essential problem: the blocker is after the caller loop, so its statement cleanup should already have run. The decisive error is comparing heaps while the entire caller/module activation remains live.\\\\n\\\\n### Required correction\\\\n\\\\nPort the Python fixture’s measurement protocol (`test/yang/python/antlr/e2e_c2_test.clj:1228-1248`):\\\\n\\\\n1. Run the PHP program **to normal completion**, without injecting the blocker.\\\\n2. Preserve the suspended `h` through its deliberate `$it->self = $it` cycle.\\\\n3. Locate that one suspended generator in the final heap.\\\\n4. Call `engine/collect` with it as an extra root.\\\\n5. Assert equality of both cell count and deep content size at N=10 and N=1000.\\\\n\\\\nAfter normal module exit, PHP’s CV and temporary cleanup must remove the caller’s ownership (`docs/design/yang.php.md:399-401`, `:673-676`, `:712-738`), leaving the cycle-rooted generator and its genuinely live delegation state. This is the same isolation strategy already used by the passing Python test.\\\\n\\\\n### Generator semantics relied upon\\\\n\\\\n- A suspended generator legitimately retains its current frame, CVs, continuation, current/key, and delegate. Neither `$i` incrementing nor repeated `yield from` requires retaining every historical yield or caller.\\\\n- `%capture` may retain a fixed stale base; **growth per yield is explicitly rejected** by ruling 7 (`docs/design/yang.antlr.md:1971-1984`).\\\\n- Generator destruction releases CVs without running pending `finally` blocks; that does not justify per-iteration retention (`docs/design/yang.php.md:341-348`).\\\\n- Tracing follows continuation and closure payloads, so the existing deep-size measurement is appropriate.\\\\n\\\\n**Engineer round:** change only `live-after-collection` to use a final VM state, as Python does. Keep the N=10/N=1000 equality assertion unchanged. Do not change the generator runtime or cleanup code on the basis of this failing fixture. If the corrected fixture still grows, that result—not the current one—would justify a runtime leak investigation.\\\"}\\n{\\\"role\\\":\\\"meta\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"session.resume_hint\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"session_858c39c2-7881-4a2b-b649-c6707fe0c4ce\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"kimi -r session_858c39c2-7881-4a2b-b649-c6707fe0c4ce\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"To resume this session: kimi -r session_858c39c2-7881-4a2b-b649-c6707fe0c4ce\\\"}\\ntest/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.clj:129:(defn run-raw\\ntest/yang/php/antlr/generators_test.clj:36:    (is (= \\\"01\\\" (:php/out (h/run-raw\\ntest/yang/php/antlr/generators_test.clj:39:    (is (= \\\"23\\\" (:php/out (h/run-raw\\ntest/yang/php/antlr/generators_test.clj:42:    (is (= \\\"aabc\\\" (:php/out (h/run-raw\\ntest/yang/php/antlr/generators_test.clj:45:    (is (= \\\"43s\\\" (:php/out (h/run-raw\\ntest/yang/php/antlr/generators_test.clj:60:(def ^:private final-vms\\ntest/yang/php/antlr/generators_test.clj:73:(defn- deep-size\\ntest/yang/php/antlr/generators_test.clj:105:        blocked ((get final-vms k) ast (vm/ast->datoms ast))]\\ntest/yang/php/antlr/generators_test.clj:109:                                (when (and (= \\\"h\\\" (get-in value [:gen :name]))\\ntest/yang/php/antlr/generators_test.clj:110:                                           (= :suspended (get-in value [:gen :state])))\\ntest/yang/php/antlr/generators_test.clj:114:          (let [heap (:heap (engine/collect blocked roots))]\\ntest/yang/php/antlr/generators_test.clj:116:             (deep-size (mapv :value (vals heap)))]))))))\\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:3721:           (if (not (nil? (get (php/obj-state o) :gen)))\\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:3994:           (if (nil? (get (php/obj-state o) :gen))\\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:4277:    [php/gen-state (fn [g] (get (php/obj-state g) :gen))]\\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:4280:       (do (cell/set! (get g :php/obj) (assoc (php/obj-state g) :gen s)) s))]\\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:4282:    [php/make-generator\\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:4321:           (php/set-handlers! (php/frame :generator (fn [e] (php/gen-fail g e)) nil))\\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:4409:       (let [s (get (php/obj-state g) :gen)]\\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:4452:         (if (if (= (php/kind v) :obj) (not (nil? (get (php/obj-state v) :gen))) false)\\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:4494:               (do (if (nil? (get (php/obj-state it) :gen))\\n(ns yang.php.antlr.generators-test\\n  \\\"P4 S8 generators, live iteration and protocol integration on the JVM.\\\"\\n  (:require\\n    [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\\n    [yang.core.uast :as u]\\n    [yang.php.antlr.e2e-harness :as h]\\n    [yang.php.antlr.programs-p4 :as p4]\\n    [yang.tails :as tails]\\n    [yin.vm :as vm]\\n    [yin.vm.debruijn.register :as rvm]\\n    [yin.vm.debruijn.stack :as dvm]\\n    [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\\n    [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]\\n    [yin.vm.semantic.derive :as derive]\\n    [yin.vm.semantic.linearize :as sr-linearize]\\n    [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]\\n    [yin.vm.values :as values])\\n  (:import\\n    [java.util IdentityHashMap]))\\n\\n\\n(def ^:private vms [:ast-walker :semantic :stack :register])\\n\\n\\n(deftest generator-fixtures-on-every-vm-test\\n  (doseq [{:keys [id source out]} p4/generators-v1]\\n    (testing (name id)\\n      (let [results (h/run-php source)]\\n        (is (not (contains? results :diagnostics)) (pr-str results))\\n        (doseq [k vms]\\n          (is (= out (get results k)) (str (name id) \\\" on \\\" k)))))))\\n\\n\\n(deftest iteration-protocols-test\\n  (testing \\\"Iterator drives foreach directly\\\"\\n    (is (= \\\"01\\\" (:php/out (h/run-raw\\n                            \\\"<?php class I implements Iterator { private $i=0; function rewind(): void {$this->i=0;} function valid(): bool {return $this->i<2;} function current(): mixed {return $this->i;} function key(): mixed {return $this->i;} function next(): void {$this->i++;} } foreach(new I as $v) echo $v;\\\")))))\\n  (testing \\\"IteratorAggregate supplies the live iterator\\\"\\n    (is (= \\\"23\\\" (:php/out (h/run-raw\\n                            \\\"<?php class I implements Iterator {private $i=2;function rewind():void{}function valid():bool{return $this->i<4;}function current(){return $this->i;}function key(){return $this->i;}function next():void{$this->i++;}} class A implements IteratorAggregate {function getIterator():Iterator{return new I;}} foreach(new A as $v)echo $v;\\\")))))\\n  (testing \\\"property iteration filters visibility from the calling scope\\\"\\n    (is (= \\\"aabc\\\" (:php/out (h/run-raw\\n                              \\\"<?php class P {public $a='a'; protected $b='b'; private $c='c'; function f(){foreach($this as $v)echo $v;}} $p=new P;foreach($p as $v)echo $v;$p->f();\\\")))))\\n  (testing \\\"ArrayAccess reads by value; Countable and Stringable dispatch\\\"\\n    (is (= \\\"43s\\\" (:php/out (h/run-raw\\n                             \\\"<?php class A implements ArrayAccess, Countable, Stringable {function offsetExists($x):bool{return true;} function offsetGet($x){return 4;} function offsetSet($x,$v):void{} function offsetUnset($x):void{} function count():int{return 3;} function __toString():string{return 's';}} $a=new A;echo $a[0],count($a),(string)$a;\\\"))))))\\n\\n\\n(def ^:private opts\\n  {:make-stream tu/make-stream\\n   :capability-secret tu/secret\\n   :primitives vm/primitives\\n   :modules (h/host-registry)})\\n\\n\\n(def ^:private load-semantic\\n  (vm/fresh-code-loader semantic/load-ast vm/ast-contract))\\n\\n\\n(def ^:private final-vms\\n  {:ast-walker (fn [ast _] (vm/eval (tu/create-vm opts) ast))\\n   :semantic (fn [_ datoms] (vm/run (load-semantic (semantic/create-vm opts) datoms)))\\n   :stack (fn [ast _]\\n            (vm/run (dvm/create-vm\\n                      (:image (derive/stack-image (:vector (sr-linearize/project ast))))\\n                      (assoc opts :contract vm/stack-contract))))\\n   :register (fn [ast _]\\n               (vm/run (rvm/create-vm\\n                         (derive/register-image (:vector (sr-linearize/project ast)))\\n                         (assoc opts :contract vm/register-contract))))})\\n\\n\\n(defn- deep-size\\n  \\\"Count shared compound values once, including closure/continuation payloads.\\\"\\n  [x]\\n  (let [seen (IdentityHashMap.)]\\n    (loop [work [x], size 0]\\n      (if (empty? work)\\n        size\\n        (let [x (peek work)\\n              work (pop work)\\n              compound? (or (values/host-typed? x) (coll? x))]\\n          (if (and compound? (.put seen x true))\\n            (recur work size)\\n            (recur (cond\\n                     (values/host-typed? x) (conj work (values/payload x))\\n                     (map? x) (into (into work (keys x)) (vals x))\\n                     (coll? x) (into work x)\\n                     :else work)\\n                   (inc size))))))))\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ncollab/orch-lane/1794950000000-engineer-p8-final-items.muse-spark-1.3-contributor.stdout.log:9:- Provenance: all 6 slow-gap records in [phpt_quick_mismatch_manifest.edn](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p8/test/yang/php/antlr/phpt_quick_mismatch_manifest.edn) carry a one-line `:measured-at` map — `bug40809` points at tree `dbe9e072` / `~/ci/rm-40809-long.log`, the rest at `06cd429f` / `~/ci/rm-phpt-quick.log`. (`bug44069`/`bug63055` have no records left to annotate; both were removed after passing.)\ncollab/orch-lane/1794950000000-engineer-p8-final-items.muse-spark-1.3-contributor.stdout.log:10:- (a) `array_unique` defaults to `SORT_STRING` (`['1.0','1']` → `\"1.0,1\"`); the test pinning loose-equality default is fixed, with explicit `SORT_REGULAR`/`SORT_NUMERIC` pins added.\ncollab/orch-lane/1794950000000-engineer-p8-final-items.muse-spark-1.3-contributor.stdout.log:11:- (b) `json_encode` failure answers `false` with no warning; `[1]` at depth 1 fails (container counts as depth level 1, matching the decode side).\ncollab/orch-lane/1794950000000-engineer-p8-final-items.muse-spark-1.3-contributor.stdout.log:13:- (d) `EXTR_PREFIX_ONLY_IF_EXISTS` removed; mode 7 is a `ValueError`.\ncollab/orch-lane/1794950000000-engineer-p8-final-items.muse-spark-1.3-contributor.stdout.log:17:Two caveats, both noted in the findings: the cited landing-review log isn't in this checkout (citations taken from the task file; the file:line references match the tree), and at default depth 512 the encode fix allows 511 nesting levels rather than 512 — no PHP binary here to arbitrate that extreme.\ncollab/orch-lane/1794580000000-reviewer-retro-step7.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log:24:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_11\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '190,270p' docs/design/yang.php.md; sed -n '1850,1960p' docs/design/yang.php.md; sed -n '2045,2140p' docs/design/yang.php.md; sed -n '2180,2355p' docs/design/yang.php.md; sed -n '3960,4080p' docs/design/yang.antlr.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"  function creation with an uninitialized sentinel. Its initializer is an\\n  arbitrary expression evaluated **when execution first reaches the\\n  declaration** (PHP 8.3) and filled once.\\n- **The dynamic-scope profile**: a function whose body contains\\n  `include`/`require`, `$$name`, `extract`, `compact`, `get_defined_vars`,\\n  `eval`, or one-argument `parse_str` keeps its locals in a heap symbol-table\\n  dict (the precedent is Python's module namespace, owner decision 1 of\\n  `yang.antlr.md` 8.5.1). Scope analysis decides per function, and the\\n  lowering targets `php/local-get`/`php/local-set` on the dict. All other\\n  functions use cells (owner decision B8.3). The symbol table holds reference\\n  markers like any location.\\n- **The global scope** is always the `$GLOBALS` dict: a heap dict,\\n  insertion-ordered, with the superglobals pre-seeded from the request record.\\n  `$GLOBALS` is read-only as of PHP 8.1 except through its elements (corner\\n  C13).\\n\\n### 3.4 Superglobals and the request context\\n\\n- A PHP run is one task consuming one **request record** from a\\n  composition-supplied stream: `{:php.request/method :uri :query :headers\\n  :cookies :body :server :env :files}`. `php/init!` builds `$_GET`, `$_POST`,\\n  `$_COOKIE`, `$_SERVER`, `$_ENV`, `$_FILES`, `$_REQUEST` (ordered per a\\n  pinned `request_order`) and, for CLI, `$argv` and `$argc`. `$_SESSION` is a\\n  bound surface (a session-store effect), absent by default. Nothing reads\\n  ambient process or HTTP state.\\n- **Output** (`echo`, `print`, inline HTML, `printf`) appends to an output\\n  cell with the output-buffering stack; `ob_start` and `ob_get_clean` are pure\\n  prelude over that stack. The top level flushes ordered `:php.response/body`\\n  records on the response stream. `header()`, `http_response_code` and\\n  `setcookie` produce `:php.response/header` records, refused after the first\\n  body flush with PHP's warning text.\\n- `exit` and `die` are an escape to the task root, followed by the shutdown\\n  sequence (row 22).\\n- Cross-request leakage is impossible by construction: one task per request\\n  and no store writes for guest state.\\n\\n### 3.5 Coercion, comparison and arithmetic\\n\\n- **Loose equality** is the PHP 8 comparison table, pinned as a fixture matrix\\n  over every pair of `null`, `true`, `false`, `0`, `1`, `-1`, `\\\"0\\\"`, `\\\"\\\"`,\\n  `\\\"1\\\"`, `\\\"01\\\"`, `\\\"1e1\\\"`, `\\\"10\\\"`, `\\\"abc\\\"`, `\\\" 1\\\"`, `\\\"1 \\\"`, `[]`, `[0]`, `0.0`,\\n  `NAN`, `INF`, an object, and a `Stringable`. For example `0 == \\\"\\\"`, `0 ==\\n  []` and `\\\"\\\" == []` are false in PHP 8, while `0 == \\\"0\\\"`, `\\\"\\\" == null`, `[]\\n  == false`, `\\\"1\\\" == \\\"01\\\"`, `\\\"10\\\" == \\\"1e1\\\"` and `100 == \\\"1e2\\\"` are true.\\n  Number versus numeric string compares numerically; number versus non-numeric\\n  string compares as strings, so `0 == \\\"a\\\"` is false. Arrays compare by key\\n  and value; objects by property, or by identity for `===`.\\n- `<=>` uses the same ordering; `===` requires identical type and value,\\n  arrays element-wise, objects the same handle.\\n- **Numeric strings** (`is_numeric`) allow leading and trailing whitespace\\n  (8.0) and exponent forms. Leading-numeric strings in arithmetic warn (`\\\"5\\n  apples\\\" + 1` warns and gives 6); non-numeric ones throw `TypeError`. String\\n  increment is supported (`\\\"a\\\"++` is `\\\"b\\\"`, `\\\"Az\\\"++` is `\\\"Ba\\\"`).\\n- **Integer overflow converts to float**: every integer operator goes through\\n  the exact integer module and demotes to float64 when the exact result leaves\\n  `[-2^63, 2^63-1]` (`PHP_INT_MAX + 1` is a float). This is the one place C3's\\n  promotion-before-overflow is used to detect rather than to promote.\\n- `/` yields an int only when exact, else a float. `%` is int-only:\\n  `PHP_INT_MIN % -1` is `0`, and `% 0` throws `DivisionByZeroError`.\\n  `intdiv(PHP_INT_MIN, -1)` throws `ArithmeticError`, and `intdiv(x, 0)`\\n  throws `DivisionByZeroError`. `fmod` never throws. `**` is an int when exact\\n  and in range, else a float, via the pinned `fpow`.\\n- **Float to string**: `echo` uses `precision=14` (`%.14G`, so `echo 0.1+0.2`\\n  prints `0.3`); `var_dump`, `var_export` and `json_encode` use\\n  `serialize_precision=-1` (the shortest round trip, `integer/float-digits`).\\n  Fourteen-significant-digit rounding needs exact decimal rounding of a\\n  binary64: a prelude function over `integer`'s exact decomposition, with no\\n  new kernel (an `integer` version bump only if measured too slow).\\n\\n### 3.6 Null\\n\\n`:php/null` is the only null. `??` and `?->` test it; `isset` is \\\"bound and\\nnot null\\\"; `empty` is falsiness; `unset` unbinds.\\n\\n### 3.7 Classes, interfaces, traits and enums\\n\\n- A class is a cell `{:php/type :class :name :parent :interfaces #{}\\n  :constants :static-props (cells) :props-decl :methods {name {:code\\n  :visibility :static? :abstract? :final? :declaring-class}} :abstract?\\n  :final? :readonly?}`. Instances are object cells (section 10.1).\\n- **Traits** are copied into the class descriptor at declaration time (class\\n+--------------------------+-------------------------------------+-----------+\\n| PHP number model         | int = exact integer bounded at 2^63 |           |\\n|                          | with overflow to float (detected by |           |\\n|                          | exact promotion, demoted by rule);  |           |\\n|                          | float = float64 content (carrier on |           |\\n|                          | JS); echo at precision 14, var_dump |           |\\n|                          | shortest; array keys coerce         |           |\\n|                          | int-like strings and floats to int  |           |\\n+--------------------------+-------------------------------------+-----------+\\n| Class-based OO (existing | Class descriptors in cells, traits  | PHP (with |\\n| row, PHP entry           | copied at declaration, interfaces   | Java,     |\\n| qualified)               | as dispatch contracts, runtime      | Python)   |\\n|                          | visibility against a class context  |           |\\n+--------------------------+-------------------------------------+-----------+\\n```\\n\\n## 11. include and require over the linker\\n\\n### 11.1 Units, names and inclusion\\n\\n- A PHP file compiled as unit `src/lib/util.php` becomes linker module\\n  `phpm.src$lib$util` (injective mangling of the normalized relative path; `/`\\n  and `.` become `$`-escapes). Its shape is Python's: `(do (require 'php)\\n  (yin/def spec {:path \\\"src/lib/util.php\\\" :strict-types 0}) (yin/def body (fn\\n  [%scope %ctx] ...)))`.\\n- `include 'x.php'` with a **literal** path (after constant folding of\\n  `__DIR__ . '/x.php'`, which the lowering performs because `__DIR__` is the\\n  unit's declared path, not a filesystem fact) lowers to the I4-a\\n  statement-time delivery thunk. The body runs in the **including scope**: it\\n  receives the including scope's symbol table, which is why an including\\n  function is on the dynamic-scope profile (at top level it is `$GLOBALS`).\\n  The body's `return` value is the expression's value, else `1`. `_once`\\n  consults the included-files dict.\\n- A computed path emits the lowering warning `:yang.php/computed-include-path`\\n  and uses the composition's literal path map at run time. A mapped path\\n  delivers by its published unit name; an unmapped path follows the missing\\n  include behaviour and records `:yang.php/computed-path-unmapped`.\\n- Conditional declarations inside included files execute in place, as in PHP.\\n- Cycles of `include` are a runtime matter (the included-files dict), not a\\n  linker cycle: static `include` edges are pinned in `:requires` only for\\n  delivery, and SCC publication handles mutual pins.\\n- **Namespaces** are compile-time; nothing links per namespace.\\n\\n### 11.2 Autoload\\n\\n`spl_autoload_register` with a guest callable is supported when the\\ncomposition also publishes the `phpm.$classmap` module. Its `classes` export\\nmaps lower-cased class names to normalized unit paths; its `paths` export\\nmaps those paths (and any additional paths selected by the composition) to\\ndelivery thunks. The autoloader then runs on a class miss and may `require`\\nonly literal paths in that map. Composer's generated class map is admissible\\nas data; its filesystem resolution is not (owner decision B8.7).\\n\\n### 11.3 Missing includes: two stages, two meanings\\n\\n1. **Publication**: every static `include`/`require` edge with a literal path\\n   must be pinned to a concrete address. A target absent from the unit set and\\n   from `published` is refused `:unpublished-import` by the lifted publisher\\n   (`yang.antlr.md` 8.5.6: \\\"publication still requires a concrete address\\\").\\n   There is **no** publication-time representation of an optional absent\\n   include; that is the known-gaps ledger's open item\\n   (\\\"publication-time-unavailable optional imports cannot be represented\\n   without concrete segment pins\\\"), not solved here (owner decision B8.10).\\n2. **Run time**: \\\"missing\\\" means the pinned content is unavailable or its\\n   delivery is refused (`:absent` with `:address`, a mismatch, an untrusted\\n   principal). `include` and `include_once` emit PHP's two warning records\\n   and yield `false`; `require` and `require_once` emit the first warning and\\n   throw `Error` with PHP's fatal text. The warning text retains the written\\n   kind. A refused path is not added to the included-files dict, so a later\\n   `_once` retries delivery. Each record carries the structured refusal under\\n   `:yang.php/refusal`.\\n\\n## 12. Safepoints\\n\\n- `:loop` and `:call` hooks (`phpsp`) serve signals: `pcntl_signal` handlers\\n  run at hooks via `stream/poll!` on a signal stream, and\\n  `pcntl_async_signals` is the default and only mode. A recursion-depth bound\\n  is available if a composition wants one (PHP has none; default off).\\n- `max_execution_time` and `set_time_limit` are wall-clock in PHP and so\\n  nondeterministic: the profile offers a deterministic **safepoint-count\\n  budget** instead, raising the fatal with PHP's text, a recorded departure\\n  (owner decision B8.5, corner C21). A composition may supply one non-negative\\n  integer budget per run; omission means unlimited. Each entry to a `:loop` or\\n  `:call` hook consumes one unit, and the hook after the last available unit\\n  raises `PHP Fatal error:  Maximum execution time of 30 seconds exceeded`.\\n  This operational fatal is not guest-catchable and skips shutdown functions\\n  and destructors. It bounds execution between hooks, not wall-clock time or\\n  blocking host operations; no generic VM instructions are charged.\\n- **Statement ticks** (`declare(ticks=N)`, `register_tick_function`) need\\n  `:line` sites before non-lambda statement nodes. `yang.safepoint` currently\\n  refuses a selected site that is not a `:lambda` (`site-not-lambda`), and\\n  `:line` insertion is safepoint slice 3, which Python tracing also needs.\\n  Ticks therefore **depend on the shared `:line` extension**: P7 splits into\\n  P7-a (signals, no dependency) and P7-b (ticks, behind safepoint slice 3).\\n  Neither L1 to L4 nor this frontend extends `yang.safepoint`; the extension\\n  is the safepoint seat's.\\n- No thread switches: PHP is single-threaded, and one request is one task.\\n\\n## 13. Diagnostics\\n\\nCompile time: `:yang.php/syntax`; `:yang.php/unsupported {:construct}`;\\n`:yang.php/not-php`; `:yang.php/unknown-builtin` (a warning);\\n`:yang.php/compile-error` for PHP's compile-time fatals (a function redeclared\\nin one unit, `break 0`, a duplicate parameter, `$this` reassignment, a\\npositional argument after a named one). Run time: guest warnings, notices and\\ndeprecations as records on the guest-diagnostics stream; fatals as `Error`\\nthrows; the uncaught-exception text pinned. Operational failures stay\\noperational (`yang.antlr.md` section 11).\\n\\n## 14. The differential-corpus plan\\n\\n|       | iterator (the same-table clause  |                                   |\\n|       | of rows 25 and 26; rows 54, 60,  |                                   |\\n|       | 61 and the migration and rebuild |                                   |\\n|       | clauses move to P3-c), the       |                                   |\\n|       | array-pointer builtins, `try`,   |                                   |\\n|       | `catch`, `finally`, `throw` and  |                                   |\\n|       | `match`. Row 65 is out (C25)     |                                   |\\n+-------+----------------------------------+-----------------------------------+\\n| P3-c  | iterator registry: per-table     | closes corner C26: rows 25, 26,   |\\n|       | iterator records, migration,     | 54, 60 and 61 and the two         |\\n|       | rebuild repositioning (the P3    | departure sources of C26          |\\n|       | plan's S7.2 and S7.3); lands     |                                   |\\n|       | before P4-b row 29               |                                   |\\n+-------+----------------------------------+-----------------------------------+\\n| P4    | classes, interfaces, traits,     | classes and exceptions groups; a  |\\n|       | enums, `match`, exceptions,      | `TypeError` for `f(\\\"x\\\")` with     |\\n|     