kimi's own stress-ruling contract implemented by kimi; the seat verified (safepoint 2/9/0, generators+objects 6/614/0) before landing. (2) P5 landed (93aa039b, merged 453aa72e): the request context — fixture-derived superglobals, ob_* output buffering, headers/cookies/status response records, the headers-after-output warning, exit/die, the error handler, the warnings stream, and the two-tasks-share-nothing isolation fixture; the seat verified (request-context 3/35/0, class-model 8/587/0) before landing. Both rounds carried uncommitted findings out of the worktree BEFORE removal (the recovery lesson applied). (3) The plan-of-record state: P0-P7-a and P5 are landed; remaining are P7-b (ticks, behind safepoint slice 3), P8 (legacy retirement), P9 (builtin surface slices); the P6 include/require rounds landed earlier. The xlang matrix (8/10/0) closed the cross-language conformance claim for all four frontends with the named yang.clojure<->TS skip (frontend/runtime work for the clojure track).\\\\norchestrator-logs/1793179048-yang-php-yang-typescript-glm-resume.md:734:Decisions: P5 fixtures authored with hand-derived expectations where PHP semantics are unambiguous; ambiguous ones stay :oracle :pending for the seat's recording pass.\\\\norchestrator-logs/1793179048-yang-php-yang-typescript-glm-resume.md:736:Delegates: kimi k3.1-pro (P7-a and P5, both COMPLETE and landed).\\\\norchestrator-logs/1793179048-yang-php-yang-typescript-glm-resume.md:737:Next: the P7-b/P8/P9 increments in sequence (kimi, window permitting); the yang.clojure runtime-module work (the xlang skip closure — the clojure track's call); the oracle recording pass for the P5 :pending fixtures.\\\\norchestrator-logs/1793179048-yang-php-yang-typescript-glm-resume.md:738:## 2026-11-04 0x:xx +0700 — P9 lands (91c5c8cd, merged 439ff42a): the last plan slice of yang.php section 15\\\\norchestrator-logs/1793179048-yang-php-yang-typescript-glm-resume.md:741:Done: P9 landed: the builtin surface slices (strings II,