                   | 63 ++++++++++++++++++----\\\\\\\\n test/yang/cross_lang_test.clj                      | 62 +++++++++++++++++++++\\\\\\\\n 3 files changed, 141 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"}}\\\\ncollab/orch-lane/1794580000000-reviewer-retro-step7.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log:24:{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.completed\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_11\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"sed -n '190,270p' docs/design/yang.php.md; sed -n '1850,1960p' docs/design/yang.php.md; sed -n '2045,2140p' docs/design/yang.php.md; sed -n '2180,2355p' docs/design/yang.php.md; sed -n '3960,4080p' docs/design/yang.antlr.md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"  function creation with an uninitialized sentinel. Its initializer is an\\\\\\\\n  arbitrary expression evaluated **when execution first reaches the\\\\\\\\n  declaration** (PHP 8.3) and filled once.\\\\\\\\n- **The dynamic-scope profile**: a function whose body contains\\\\\\\\n  `include`/`require`, `$$name`, `extract`, `compact`, `get_defined_vars`,\\\\\\\\n  `eval`, or one-argument `parse_str` keeps its locals in a heap symbol-table\\\\\\\\n  dict (the precedent is Python's module namespace, owner decision 1 of\\\\\\\\n  `yang.antlr.md` 8.5.1). Scope analysis decides per function, and the\\\\\\\\n  lowering targets `php/local-get`/`php/local-set` on the dict. All other\\\\\\\\n  functions use cells (owner decision B8.3). The symbol table holds reference\\\\\\\\n  markers like any location.\\\\\\\\n- **The global scope** is always the `$GLOBALS` dict: a heap dict,\\\\\\\\n  insertion-ordered, with the superglobals pre-seeded from the request record.\\\\\\\\n  `$GLOBALS` is read-only as of PHP 8.1 except through its elements (corner\\\\\\\\n  C13).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### 3.4 Superglobals and the request context\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- A PHP run is one task consuming one **request record** from a\\\\\\\\n  composition-supplied stream: `{:php.request/method :uri :query :headers\\\\\\\\n  :cookies :body :server :env :files}`. `php/init!` builds `$_GET`, `$_POST`,\\\\\\\\n  `$_COOKIE`, `$_SERVER`, `$_ENV`, `$_FILES`, `$_REQUEST` (ordered per a\\\\\\\\n  pinned `request_order`) and, for CLI, `$argv` and `$argc`. `$_SESSION` is a\\\\\\\\n  bound surface (a session-store effect), absent by default. Nothing reads\\\\\\\\n  ambient process or HTTP state.\\\\\\\\n- **Output** (`echo`, `print`, inline HTML, `printf`) appends to an output\\\\\\\\n  cell with the output-buffering stack; `ob_start` and `ob_get_clean` are pure\\\\\\\\n  prelude over that stack. The top level flushes ordered `:php.response/body`\\\\\\\\n  records on the response stream. `header()`, `http_response_code` and\\\\\\\\n  `setcookie` produce `:php.response/header` records, refused after the first\\\\\\\\n  body flush with PHP's warning text.\\\\\\\\n- `exit` and `die` are an escape to the task root, followed by the shutdown\\\\\\\\n  sequence (row 22).\\\\\\\\n- Cross-request leakage is impossible by construction: one task per request\\\\\\\\n  and no store writes for guest state.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### 3.5 Coercion, comparison and arithmetic\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- **Loose equality** is the PHP 8 comparison table, pinned as a fixture matrix\\\\\\\\n  over every pair of `null`, `true`, `false`, `0`, `1`, `-1`, `\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"0\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"`, `\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"`,\\\\\\\\n  `\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"1\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"`, `\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"01\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"`, `\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"1e1\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"`, `\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"10\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"`, `\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"abc\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"`, `\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" 1\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"`, `\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"1 \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"`, `[]`, `[0]`, `0.0`,\\\\\\\\n  `NAN`, `INF`, an object, and a `Stringable`. For example `0 == \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"`, `0 ==\\\\\\\\n  []` and `\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" == []` are false in PHP 8, while `0 == \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"0\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"`, `\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" == null`, `[]\\\\\\\\n  == false`, `\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"1\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" == \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"01\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"`, `\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"10\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" == \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"1e1\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"` and `100 == \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"1e2\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"` are true.\\\\\\\\n  Number versus numeric string compares numerically; number versus non-numeric\\\\\\\\n  string compares as strings, so `0 == \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"a\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"` is false. Arrays compare by key\\\\\\\\n  and value; objects by property, or by identity for `===`.\\\\\\\\n- `<=>` uses the same ordering; `===` requires identical type and value,\\\\\\\\n  arrays element-wise, objects the same handle.\\\\\\\\n- **Numeric strings** (`is_numeric`) allow leading and trailing whitespace\\\\\\\\n  (8.0) and exponent forms. Leading-numeric strings in arithmetic warn (`\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"5\\\\\\\\n  apples\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" + 1` warns and gives 6); non-numeric ones throw `TypeError`. String\\\\\\\\n  increment is supported (`\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"a\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"++` is `\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"b\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"`, `\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Az\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"++` is `\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Ba\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"`).\\\\\\\\n- **Integer overflow converts to float**: every integer operator goes through\\\\\\\\n  the exact integer module and demotes to float64 when the exact result leaves\\\\\\\\n  `[-2^63, 2^63-1]` (`PHP_INT_MAX + 1` is a float). This is the one place C3's\\\\\\\\n  promotion-before-overflow is used to detect rather than to promote.\\\\\\\\n- `/` yields an int only when exact, else a float. `%` is int-only:\\\\\\\\n  `PHP_INT_MIN % -1` is `0`, and `% 0` throws `DivisionByZeroError`.\\\\\\\\n  `intdiv(PHP_INT_MIN, -1)` throws `ArithmeticError`, and `intdiv(x, 0)`\\\\\\\\n  throws `DivisionByZeroError`. `fmod` never throws. `**` is an int when exact\\\\\\\\n  and in range, else a float, via the pinned `fpow`.\\\\\\\\n- **Float to string**: `echo` uses `precision=14` (`%.14G`, so `echo 0.1+0.2`\\\\\\\\n  prints `0.3`); `var_dump`, `var_export` and `json_encode` use\\\\\\\\n  `serialize_precision=-1` (the shortest round trip, `integer/float-digits`).\\\\\\\\n  Fourteen-significant-digit rounding needs exact decimal rounding\n... 2482478 bytes omitted ...\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$OUT/summary.txt\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nxargs -P \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PAR\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" -I{} bash -c \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"run_ns {}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" < \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$HOME/ci/pertest-ns.txt\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\necho \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"done $(date +%H:%M:%S)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" >> \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$OUT/summary.txt\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n## Remote test servers: shiva and jupiter\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nTwo Linux x86_64 servers run the full suite faster than a laptop. Both are\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nreached over SSH as `sto` with key authentication, and both have `mise`, `tmux`\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nand `git`.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| Host | Cores / RAM | Toolchain state (server snapshot checked 2026-10-11; repo selection comes from `mise.toml`) |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n|---|---|---|\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| `shiva.stigmergy.systems` | 24 / 62 GB | Server snapshot: java 21, clojure 1.12.4.1602, node 25.6.1, babashka, cljstyle, zprint, flutter 3.47.1. The repo's `mise.toml` selects Flutter `latest` on beta, not a fixed version. Activate the repo toolchain before running any lane. |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| `jupiter.stigmergy.systems` | 48 / 62 GB | Server snapshot (rechecked 2026-10-29): java 21, clojure 1.12.4.1602, node 25.6.1, babashka, cljstyle, zprint, flutter 3.47.8 (the stale hand-symlinked 3.41.9 was replaced via `mise install flutter@3.47.8` after it failed to compile `dart:ui`-using cljd namespaces; if the Dart lane dies in the cljd compile, check `mise ls flutter` first). Tri-host quick tier verified green on 2026-10-29 (see Measured times). |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Never test in `~/workspace/datomworld` on either host.** It is a working copy\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nthat is behind origin (shiva: 45 commits behind on 2026-10-11) and belongs to its\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nowner. Use a scratch clone under `~/ci/` and leave the working copy alone.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n### Get the code there: push to origin, never rsync\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nRsyncing a worktree over the WAN ran at about 150 KB/s (576 MB of tracked files\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nwould take about an hour), and an unanchored `--exclude build` also dropped source\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ndirectories named `build`, `out` and `target`. Both hosts reach GitHub, so push the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nbranch from the laptop (a feature branch, never master), make one scratch clone on\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nthe host from its existing checkout (a local clone takes seconds), and fetch:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```sh\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n# once per host: a separate scratch clone, not the working copy\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nssh shiva.stigmergy.systems 'set -e; mkdir -p ~/ci; cd ~/workspace/datomworld;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  URL=$(git remote get-url origin);\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  git clone -q --no-checkout ~/workspace/datomworld ~/ci/datomworld-<name>;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  cd ~/ci/datomworld-<name>; git remote set-url origin \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$URL\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\";\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  git fetch -q origin; git checkout -q --detach origin/<branch>'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nTo test another branch later, fetch and check it out in the scratch clone with\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n`git fetch origin` then `git checkout --detach origin/<branch>`. A branch that\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nwas never pushed cannot be tested remotely.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n### Activate the toolchain in the right order\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nA non-interactive `ssh host cmd` does not load the shell profile, so `mise` and its\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ntools are not on PATH. In a script, do this in exactly this order, after the `cd`\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ninto the clone:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```sh\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nexport PATH=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$HOME/.local/bin:/snap/bin:$PATH\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"   # mise: ~/.local/bin on shiva, /snap/bin on jupiter\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ncd ~/ci/datomworld-<name>\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nmise trust >/dev/null 2>&1                       # trust is per path; a fresh clone is untrusted\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nmise install                                    # install versions selected by this checkout's mise.toml\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\neval \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$(mise env -s bash)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"                       # puts the repo-selected tools on PATH\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nmise current flutter                            # verify the selected Flutter version\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nActivating mise before the `cd` and `mise trust` leaves the repo-selected tools\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n(flutter in particular) off PATH: the Dart lane then dies in seconds with \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Can't\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nfind flutter on PATH\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", and so does `bb build:yin-repl-peer`.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n### Which lanes may overlap (reconciling the one-lane-set rule)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"One lane set at a time\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" and \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"one Dart lane at a time\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" are per-machine rules about\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nCPU: they exist because a laptop has 8 cores. They are not a rule about repos.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n`test.subsystems.md` section 5 item 6 says the same (\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"on one machine where\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\navoidable\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"). On shiva (24 cores) and jupiter (48) the cores are not the limit, so\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nlanes may overlap, with these limits:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- **JVM and Dart lanes must not share one clone.** `src/dev/affected.clj`\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  (`serialized-pairs`, the `[:clj :cljd]` pair) serializes them whenever a JVM test\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  runs the cljd compiler, and some do (`yin.repl.build-test`,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  `yin.vm.linker.cross-host-transfer-test`, `dao.stream.ws-project-cross-jvm-test`);\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  the compiler writes the clone's `lib/cljd-out` and `build/`. A second scratch clone\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  gives the Dart lane its own copies, so the two lanes then overlap safely. This is\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  by the design's own reasoning (\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"each worktree owns its own `cljd-out`\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"), not yet\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  verified by a measured run.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- **JVM and Node may share a clone.** Node writes `target/` and `.shadow-cljs/`; the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  JVM lane only reads `target/yin-repl.js`.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- **One Dart lane per host at a time**, even across clones: the lane shards up to\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  `min(8, cores)` Flutter processes and shares the host's Flutter cache.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- **Different branches in different clones** are independent, so two branches may\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  run on one host if its cores and RAM allow (62 GB each).\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Do not treat this as permission to overlap lanes on the laptop.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe first run on shiva (2026-10-11) overlapped JVM and Dart in one clone before\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nthis rule was written down; its results are advisory until repeated with a\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nseparate Dart clone.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n### The full run\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nRun long jobs inside `tmux` so the SSH session can drop. The script below does the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nserial prerequisites once, then runs the JVM and Node lanes in the first clone and\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nthe Dart lane in a second clone, all concurrently, with the same commands the `bb`\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ntasks use (the `bb test` task runs them one after another), and records each\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nlane's exit code and seconds. Make the Dart clone the same way as the first, at the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nsame commit, with a name like `~/ci/datomworld-<name>-dart`:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```sh\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n# ~/ci/run-full.sh <jvm-node-clone> [<dart-clone>]   (both hosts run all three lanes; a second clone for Dart is recommended)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nset -u\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nexport PATH=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$HOME/.local/bin:/snap/bin:$PATH\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nDART=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"${2:-}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ncd \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$1\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" || exit 2\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nmise trust >/dev/null 2>&1\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\neval \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$(mise env -s bash)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nLOG=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$1/target-ci\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"; mkdir -p \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$LOG\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nts() { date +%H:%M:%S; }\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\necho \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"start $(ts) $(git rev-parse --short HEAD)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" | tee \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$LOG/summary.txt\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nnpm ci --silent >\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$LOG/npm.log\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" 2>&1               && echo \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"npm ok $(ts)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" | tee -a \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$LOG/summary.txt\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nbb build:yin-repl-node >\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$LOG/build-node.log\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" 2>&1 && echo \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"node repl built $(ts)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" | tee -a \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$LOG/summary.txt\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nbb gen:antlr >\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$LOG/antlr.log\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" 2>&1         && echo \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"antlr ok $(ts)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" | tee -a \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$LOG/summary.txt\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nbb build:yin-repl-peer >\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$LOG/build-peer.log\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" 2>&1 && echo \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"dart peer built $(ts)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" | tee -a \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$LOG/summary.txt\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nlane() { name=$1; shift; s=$(date +%s); \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$@\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" >\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$LOG/$name.log\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" 2>&1; rc=$?\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n         echo \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$name rc=$rc secs=$(( $(date +%s)-s )) $(ts)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" | tee -a \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$LOG/summary.txt\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"; }\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nlane jvm  clojure -M:test -e :slow &\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nlane node clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile test &\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nif [ -n \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$DART\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" ]; then                            # its own clone (own lib/cljd-out, build/)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  ( cd \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$DART\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" && mise trust >/dev/null 2>&1 && eval \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$(mise env -s bash)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    bb build:yin-repl-peer >\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$LOG/build-peer-dart.log\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" 2>&1\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    lane dart bb src/dev/cljd_agg.clj ) &\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nfi\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nwait\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\necho \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"done $(ts)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" | tee -a \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$LOG/summary.txt\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```sh\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nssh <host> 'tmux new-session -d -s ci-full \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"bash -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"~/ci/run-full.sh ~/ci/datomworld-<name> ~/ci/datomworld-<name>-dart > ~/ci/run-full.out 2>&1\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nWatch it: `ssh <host>`, then `tmux attach -t ci-full` (detach with `Ctrl-b d`; do not\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\npress Ctrl-C inside it), or `tail -f ~/ci/datomworld-<name>/target-ci/{jvm,node,dart}.log`\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nand `cat .../summary.txt` (all logs and the summary are in the first clone). The session's own output is empty by design: the lanes\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nwrite to the logs. The JVM lane uses `-e :slow`, so it skips `^:slow` tests, like\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n`bb test:clj`. For the slow set use `-i :slow` (or `bb test:slow`); the slow C4\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nscanner row took about 11-19 minutes on the JVM and about 79 minutes on Node\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n(measured 2026-10-11).\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n### Known differences from the laptop\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- **`dao.stream.datagram.dart-test/refusals-and-lifecycle-events` fails on Linux.**\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  The assertion \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"a bind on a taken port deposits bind-failed\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" gets no `bind-failed`\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  event. A second UDP bind on a taken port evidently behaves differently on Linux\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  than on macOS (inferred, not confirmed). The test is in `dao.stream`, which the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  semantic-register slices do not touch: treat it as a known Linux-only failure,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  not a regression, until it is fixed or guarded.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- A JVM lane started before the Dart peer is built skips the Dart-peer tests with a\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  printed notice. The script builds the peer first so they run.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Both hosts run other work (a QEMU guest and rustdesk on shiva); idle load is\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  under 1, but timings are not a clean benchmark.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n### Measured times (first runs, 2026-10-11, commit 84c7c9b7, all lanes concurrent)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nShiva, Dart lane: 1054 s (17.5 min) cold, with the JVM and Node lanes running beside\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nit, against about 9 minutes on the 8-core laptop run alone. Prerequisites (`npm ci`,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nNode REPL, ANTLR) took about 30 s; the Dart peer 91 s. JVM and Node lane times are\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nnot recorded yet: fill them in from `summary.txt` after a completed run. Running the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nlanes concurrently on one host did not make the Dart lane faster, so count on the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nextra cores and a free laptop, and measure before relying on a speedup.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n### Jupiter verification run (2026-10-29, commit 7c0a078f, scratch clone, sequential lanes)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nFirst full tri-host verification of jupiter. Prerequisites (npm ci, Node REPL,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nANTLR via `gen:antlr`, Dart peer) all succeeded; the stale 3.41.9 Flutter was\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nreplaced with 3.47.8 before the Dart lane. Results: **JVM quick tier\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n(`test:quick-sharded`, 12 workers) rc=0 in 702 s** (cold, every shard green);\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Node quick tier rc=0 in 4583 s** (all tests pass, but roughly 15x the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nlaptop \\\\u2014 route Node lanes to the laptop or shiva); **Dart quick tier\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nrc=1 in 1495 s with the ONLY failure the documented known Linux-only red**\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n(`dao.stream.datagram.dart-test/refusals-and-lifecycle-events`, same\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ntaken-port/bind-failed signature recorded above). Routing summary: jupiter\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nis the preferred JVM/sharding box (48 cores); Node stays off it when wall\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ntime matters; Dart works on either host. Timings are single cold runs, not\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nmedians, and two foreign QEMU guests idle on the host.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nOne exception to the concurrency above: never run two lanes that both trigger\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n`gen:antlr` (the quick `test:cljs`/`test:cljd` tasks) in the SAME worktree at the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nsame time \\\\u2014 they race on `build/antlr` and `lib/antlr` and fail with\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Patch does not apply\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" or \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Generated sources differ from the recorded digests\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\".\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nRun them sequentially, or in separate clones (as the slow-tier harness does).\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe fix after a collision is `rm -rf build/antlr lib/antlr` and a rerun; the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ngenerator is not idempotent over an already-patched tree. Corroborated twice in\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\none week (the M3 round and the C3 completion round, 2026-10-18).\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n### Remote agent execution (delegate CLIs on shiva and jupiter)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nOwner relay, 2026-10-24: the delegate agent CLIs \\\\u2014 `claude`, `codex`, `glm` \\\\u2014\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nare installed and usable **on the remote hosts themselves**, not only from the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\norchestrator's laptop. This generalizes this section from \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"run tests remotely\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nover SSH\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" to \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"delegate whole work agents remotely\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": a heavy implementation or\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nverification leg (test lanes, native builds, fault-injection runs, multi-hour\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nsuites) can be executed by a delegate agent running on the server, keeping the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\norchestrator's laptop unloaded.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe pattern (composed from the rules above plus the delegate-invocation\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nreference):\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n1. **Land the branch on origin first** (push from the laptop; never rsync) and\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   prepare the scratch clone per \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Get the code there\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\".\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n2. **Start a named tmux session** for the task; run the agent inside it with\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   the toolchain activated *inside* the tmux command (`eval \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$(mise env -s\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   bash)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"` after the `cd` \\\\u2014 the non-interactive SSH shell does not have it).\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   A fresh clone hits mise's interactive trust prompt, which blocks the whole\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   session until answered via `tmux send-keys`; pre-empt it with `mise trust`\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   inside the same command.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n3. **The remote agent works in the clone**: implement, build, run lanes,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   write its findings artifact \\\\u2014 the same brief form as any delegate dispatch\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   (role template, bounded file ownership, deliverable path), just executing\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   on the host. Long jobs survive SSH drops because of tmux.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n4. **The orchestrator polls detached files, never the pane** (pane captures\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   carry control characters that make output look empty): rc files, summary\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   logs and `ls *.flag` sentinels written by the run.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n5. **Division of labor**: bookkeeping and polling are orchestrator SSH\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   one-liners; execution belongs to the remote agent. Do not run heavy lanes\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   from the orchestrator's laptop while a remote agent owns the same gate.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n6. **Same trust rules as any delegate**: remote execution does not waive\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   Workflow steps 6\\\\u20137 of the orchestrator role \\\\u2014 artifacts are verified, and\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   review before commit applies to remote-produced work identically.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   Session-ID capture and resume rules from the delegate-invocation reference\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   apply per host (each host's `~/.claude`, `~/.codex` store is its own).\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nKnown state: `claude` and `codex` verified working on shiva (2026-10-24, the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\njolt canonical-fixes verification ran there); `glm` reported available by the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nowner on both hosts, not yet exercised. Both hosts are toolchain-verified for\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nthe full tri-host suite (jupiter verified 2026-10-29 \\\\u2014 see Measured times;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nits 3.41.9 Flutter was replaced with 3.47.8, and model availability per\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nhost is governed by `routing-status.md`, not this file).\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n## Testing Philosophy & TDD\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nWrite tests before implementing features (TDD).\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nTests define the contract and expected behavior. Implementation follows from the tests, not the other way around.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nWhen implementing a feature or fix:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n1. **Red phase**: Write the test first \\\\u2014 define what should happen.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n2. **Green phase**: Implement the minimum code to pass the test.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n3. **Refactor phase**: Refactor if needed while keeping tests green.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThis ensures code is testable by design and implementation matches actual requirements.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n## Debugging Malformed CLJ / EDN / CLJS\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nA single missing bracket can silently break an entire file. The compiler may still succeed, with subsequent forms nesting inside the broken one.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n1. **Run clj-kondo first**:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   ```sh\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   clj -M:kondo --lint path/to/file.cljs\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   ```\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n2. **If clj-kondo reports a mismatch, write a bracket-tracing script**:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   Do NOT try to eyeball-count brackets. Track a stack of `(char, line, col)` for every opener. Handle: string literals, escaped chars, and `;;` line comments.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n3. **Fix one bracket at a time, re-run checker after each fix**:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   Common patterns:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   - Hiccup vector missing `]` causes siblings to become extra arguments.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   - `defn`/`let` missing `)` causes subsequent top-level forms to nest inside.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   - Both can coexist while total bracket count is zero-sum.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n4. **After brackets balance**, rerun `clj-kondo`, then rebuild with `clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile <build>`.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n---\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ndescription: File and content format rules for datom.world \\\\u2014 .chp/.blog EDN+Hiccup files, tables in .md files, and git commit message format\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n---\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n# FORMATS\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n`.chp` and `.blog` files are EDN files with Hiccup markup.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n## Structure for .blog files\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```clojure\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n#:blog{:title \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Title Here\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n       :date #inst \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS.000-00:00\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n       :abstract [:p \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Abstract with hiccup markup...\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n       :content [:section.blog-article\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                 [:div.section-inner\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                  [:article\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                   :$blog-title\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                   :$blog-date\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                   ;; Hiccup content here\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                   ]]]}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n## Guidelines for .blog files\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Use EDN syntax with namespaced maps (`#:blog{...}`)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Use Hiccup vectors for all markup (`[:p \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"text\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]`, `[:strong \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"bold\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]`, `[:a {:href \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"...\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"} \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"link\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]`)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Never use markdown syntax\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Include `:$blog-title` and `:$blog-date` where appropriate\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Never use em dashes (\\\\u2014). Use commas, colons, periods, or parentheses instead.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n## Tables in .md files\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nTables in `.md` files (design documents, agent guides) are ASCII box tables,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nnever markdown pipe tables:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n+-------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| Rule              | Detail                                                                    |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n+===================+===========================================================================+\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| Borders           | `+`, `-`, and `|` draw the box; a `+===+` rule separates the header row   |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n|                   | from the body; every row closes with a full `+---+` border                |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n+-------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| Maximum width     | 170 columns, counted in characters (UTF-8 aware), including the borders   |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n+-------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| Column widths     | Columns that fit at their natural width stay unwrapped; wide columns      |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n|                   | share the remaining budget proportionally to their content                |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n+-------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| Wrapping          | Long cell content word-wraps onto continuation lines that carry only the  |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n|                   | wrapped column; other columns are blank on continuation lines; an         |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n|                   | unbreakable token longer than its column hard-breaks at the column edge   |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n+-------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe example table above is itself in the format: `docs/agents/team.md` and\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n`docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md` are the reference\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ninstances (the previous second instance, the v3 `yin.vm.semantic.md`, was\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ndeleted at the 2026-10-15 cutover and its replacement carries no border\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ntables).\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n## Git commit messages\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThis is a repository-wide convention, not specific to any one role. Commit\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nsubjects use:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```text\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n<type>[(<scope>)]: <lowercase imperative summary>\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n`type` is one of `docs|feat|fix|refactor|perf|test|build|chore`. An optional\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nbody explains non-obvious behavior or invariants; omit it when the subject\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nline is self-explanatory. Use no trailing period on the subject line. Merge\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ncommits are exempt from this format. Never add `Co-Authored-By`, including\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nLLM attribution, to any commit in this repository.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nWhether and when a commit is *allowed* to happen (review requirements,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nauthorization, undoing an unauthorized commit) is role-specific policy, not\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nformat \\\\u2014 see [`roles/orchestrator.md`](roles/orchestrator.md)'s Coordination\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ncontract for the orchestrator's own gating rules.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n# Slice 9 kernel differential gate \\\\u2014 BLOCKED\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThis is a failing close-out gate, not a conformance certificate. No compiler or\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nVM source was changed. No commit was made.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe 54 fixtures in `kernel_gate.edn` invoke actual pinned upstream functions on A,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nexecute the explicit context source on host Clojure on B, and compile the guest\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nsource for C-walker and C-semantic. Guest extension closures are evaluated by the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nVM; the harness supplies no host callback primitive. The original proof dispatcher\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nis assembled, rather than substituting slice 8's restricted state-step dispatcher.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nEvery fixture, including every negative, has an A/B/C-walker/C-semantic outcome in\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n`slice9_evidence.edn`. Blocked fixtures are attempted and recorded independently;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nno negative is skipped or counted as a successful guest rejection.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nResult: **4 passing fixtures, 2 mismatches, 48 blocked fixtures**. Passing fixtures\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nare `:subst-capture`, `:subst-shadow`, `:subst-three-arity`, and\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n`:unparser-guest-closure`. The compile/admission blockers occur before either C\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nlane executes those blocked programs; both lane records explicitly say so.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n## Mismatches with minimal repros\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n1. `:minimal-gensym-freshness`:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   ```clojure\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   (let [a (gensym \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"fresh\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\") b (gensym \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"fresh\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")] (= a b))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   ```\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   A and B return `false`; both C lanes return `[:yin.k/ok true]`. The guest\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   library's one-argument `gensym` constructs `G__fresh` repeatedly. This\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   dependency is reachable from `latte-kernel.typing/rebuild-type`. No fresh-name\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   correspondence can turn equality of two names into inequality.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n2. `:free-vars-local-capture`:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   ```clojure\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   (latte-kernel.syntax/free-vars\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     (latte-kernel.defenv/register-definition env\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n       (latte-kernel.defenv/->Definition 'd [] 0 'x '#{x} 'A {}) true)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     '(d))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   ```\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   A returns `#{x}`; B returns `#{}`; both C lanes return `[:yin.k/ok #{}]`.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   The upstream `free-vars` implementation uses `(second def-env)` to access\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   local definitions. The inherited context adaptation passes a context map in\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   that position. This is an A/B adaptation mismatch, independently of compilation.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n## Blocked dependencies\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Parsing reaches `butlast`, `last`, bare `nth`, and `kind/var?`, which are not\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  admitted by the supplied portable modules. Minimal independent fixtures for\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  `last`, `nth`, and `var?` are included. The parser's valid and malformed cases\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  all run on A/B, but their guest dependency closures fail admission.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Normalization reaches `last` in `nbe/evaluation` and `with-meta` in\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  `nbe/quotation-`. `:minimal-last` and `:minimal-with-meta` isolate these failures.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  Beta, transparent delta, opaque delta, and each required public normalization\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  arity have named fixtures; no host normalization is substituted for C.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Typing reaches the actual `typing/unfold-implicit` `try/catch`, including\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  `.getMessage`, `ex-data`, and exception bindings. Slice 8's already-typed\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  extension adapter does not replace this full typed-argument path. The two\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  implicit fixtures use actual guest closure source and remain blocked.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- `typing/type-of-ascribe` is declared but has no definition in the pinned\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  upstream source and no manifest entry. `:typing-ascription` also exposes the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  upstream unbound-function failure on A. It is never treated as a successful\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  type rejection by C.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Full proof elaboration/checking reaches `proof/+opacity-fn+`, an ambient atom\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  initialized with a closure. Yang rejects this `def` initializer under the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  outcome convention. Each affected fixture records\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  `:blocked-by [gate-proof-+opacity-fn+]` and the exact `:minimal-source`.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  The inherited partial proof-step context adapter cannot stand in for the real\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  parsing/typing dispatcher. Proof compilation separately reaches the missing\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  `string?` dependency; even `:compile-proof`'s single `:qed` script is explicitly\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  blocked by this dependency rather than treated as a successful rejection.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Upstream's error for steps after `qed` includes the host `clojure.core/meta`\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  function in its `:meta` field. Evidence explicitly marks this nonportable host\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  value; it is not normalized into an accepted portability difference. The\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  malformed scalar proof-step fixture also records its native upstream exception.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe complete source dependency graph, per-fixture closure membership, missing\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nsymbols and their owning definitions, compiler exception causes, and minimal\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ncalls are retained in `slice9_evidence.edn`. Compiler/admission/VM exceptions are\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nblockers; only actual returned `:ko`, `false`, or corresponding domain exceptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ncan satisfy negative fixtures. A test assertion checks that every completed A\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nnegative really rejects its input.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n## Manifest and coverage\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe inherited manifest contains **155 bindings, 147 functions, and 175\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nfunction/arity entries**,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nnot the plan's earlier estimate of 143 definitions. It has no admitted/excluded\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ndispositions, and its source fields are nil. Consequently an exact admitted\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nfunction/arity denominator cannot be recovered honestly from that manifest.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n`admitted-function-arity-count` is explicitly `:not-recorded-in-inherited-manifest`.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nAll 175 entries are retained as gate obligations; successful fixtures do not\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nnarrow the denominator.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe conservative, proven direct A/B/C agreement count is **2/175 arities**:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n`latte-kernel.syntax/subst` at arities 2 and 3. The successful unparser integration\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nalso executes its dependencies, but this harness does not claim an exact dynamic\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ntransitive arity count. It records `:transitive-execution-coverage :unproven`.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nAll **173 remaining unexercised-or-unproven entries** are individually listed\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nunder `:coverage :unexercised`, alongside the complete function/arity inventory.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nDependency closure membership is recorded separately and does not count as\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nexecution. This incomplete accounting itself blocks the close-out gate.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n## Reproduction and verification\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nPins: upstream LaTTe `86fca0d1d054af005cb37395eae04500d45e6279`; compiler/VM\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n`f74f2cecccfc54813671555b15e39d254debd2d9`; context adaptation v1, kernel assembly v1.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe recorded host uses Clojure 1.12.4 and Java 17.0.18. Each C execution has a\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n1,000,000-instruction budget. There is no continuation-depth claim for blocked\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nprograms.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nRun the gate:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```sh\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nclj -M:test -n yang.latte-oracle-test\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**22 tests, 988 assertions, 1 failure, 0 errors, exit 1.** The single failed\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nassertion is `test-kernel-differential-gate`: the gate must remain red while the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nabove blockers or unproven coverage remain. The inherited 21 tests passed in the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nbaseline: 968 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors. Do not remove the close-out\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nassertion to manufacture the requested zero-failure result.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nExplicitly refresh evidence from fresh A/B/C runs (normal test runs do not rewrite\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nit):\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```sh\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nclj -Sdeps '{:aliases {:gate {:main-opts [\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"-e\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"(require (quote yang.latte-oracle-test)) (println (select-keys (yang.latte-oracle-test/write-kernel-gate-evidence!) [:gate-status :counts :fixture-count :manifest-bindings :function-arity-candidates]))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]}}}' -M:test:gate\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThis evidence-writing command returns normally even when the recorded gate is\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nblocked; only the test command above is the acceptance gate.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nUnchanged regression suites:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```sh\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nclj -M:test -n yang.clojure-test -n yin.vm.macro-test -n yang.clojure.stream-eval-test -n yin.vm.store-write-audit-test\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Blocked at namespace loading**, `ClassNotFoundException:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nyang.python.antlr.gen.Python3Lexer`; no green four-suite result. The stream/REPL\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nsuite imports the frontend catalog that requires the generated Python parser.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe prerequisite attempt\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n`clj -M:antlr-gen --grammar python3 --target java` failed with\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n`java.nio.channels.UnresolvedAddressException` while retrieving required inputs.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe independent suites were then run separately:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```sh\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nclj -M:test -n yang.clojure-test -n yin.vm.macro-test -n yin.vm.store-write-audit-test\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nclj -M:test -n yin.vm.semantic.linearize-test -n yin.vm.semantic.analysis-test -n yin.vm.semantic.frame-test\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nRespectively **106 tests / 1,007 assertions** and **45 tests / 1,944 assertions**,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nboth with **0 failures and 0 errors**.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nCross-host regression availability is separate from the JVM kernel oracle:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- `bb test:changed:cljs --changed test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj test/yang/latte_oracle/kernel_gate.edn`\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  could not start: `bb` is absent (exit 127).\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Fallback `clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile test` failed before any\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  Node tests ran. `CompilerOptions` requires class-file version 65 (Java 21), but\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  the active runtime supports version 61 (Java 17). Node itself is available.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Dart/Flutter are absent from PATH. No Dart suite ran; that lane is unavailable,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  not green. Four-evaluator stream/REPL verification remains blocked as above.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- `git diff --check` passed.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n{:deps {org.clojure/core.async {:mvn/version \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"1.8.741\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n        org.clojure/tools.reader {:mvn/version \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"1.5.0\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n        ring/ring {:mvn/version \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"1.14.1\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n        com.cognitect/transit-clj {:mvn/version \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"1.0.333\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n        org.replikativ/boring {:mvn/version \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"0.1.30\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n        com.datomic/peer {:mvn/version \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"1.0.7364\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n        org.postgresql/postgresql {:mvn/version \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"42.7.3\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n        org.clojure/data.json {:mvn/version \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"2.5.0\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n        http-kit/http-kit {:mvn/version \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"2.8.0\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n        org.jsoup/jsoup {:mvn/version \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"1.18.3\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n        instaparse/instaparse {:mvn/version \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"1.5.0\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n        ;; yang.python.antlr: the runtime the generated Python3 parser runs\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n        ;; on; pinned to the tool version in :antlr-gen (they are one release)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n        org.antlr/antlr4-runtime {:mvn/version \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"4.13.2\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n        criterium/criterium {:mvn/version \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"0.4.6\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n        io.github.rctcwyvrn/blake3 {:mvn/version \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"1.3\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n        stigmergy/chp {:mvn/version \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"0.1.0-SNAPSHOT\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                       :exclusions [refactor-nrepl/refactor-nrepl]}}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n :cljd/opts {}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n ;; build/antlr/python3/classes: the generated Python3 parser, produced by\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n ;; `clj -M:antlr-gen` (antlr/python3/manifest.edn); absent until generated\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n :paths [\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"src/clj\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"src/cljc\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"src/cljs\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"src/cljd\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n         \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"build/antlr/python3/classes\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"build/antlr/php/classes\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n         \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"build/antlr/typescript/classes\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n :aliases {:clean {:extra-paths [\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"src/dev\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                   :exec-fn clean/clean}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n           :profile-btree {:extra-paths [\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"src/dev\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                           :extra-deps {persistent-sorted-set/persistent-sorted-set\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                                        {:mvn/version \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"0.3.0\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                           :main-opts [\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"-m\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"btree-bench\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n           :test {:extra-paths [\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"test\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                  :extra-deps {io.github.cognitect-labs/test-runner\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                               {:git/tag \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"v0.5.1\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" :git/sha \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"dfb30dd\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                               ;; latte-kernel: the LaTTe proof assistant's kernel,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                               ;; the differential oracle for the yang.clojure gap\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                               ;; program (pinned; MIT; dependency-free)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                               latte-kernel/latte-kernel\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                               {:git/url \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"https://github.com/latte-central/latte-kernel\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                                :git/sha \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"86fca0d1d054af005cb37395eae04500d45e6279\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                  :main-opts [\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"-m\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"cognitect.test-runner\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                  :exec-fn cognitect.test-runner.api/test}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n           :nREPL {:extra-paths [\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"test\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                   :extra-deps {nrepl/nrepl {:mvn/version \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"1.0.0\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                                cider/cider-nrepl {:mvn/version \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"0.58.0\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                   :main-opts [\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"-m\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"nrepl.cmdline\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"--middleware\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"[cider.nrepl/cider-middleware]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n           :cljs {:extra-paths [\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"test\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"src/dev\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"build/antlr/python3/js\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                  :extra-deps {thheller/shad