\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n(defn- walk-symbols\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  [form]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  (cond\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    (seq? form) (if (and (= 'quote (first form)) (= 2 (count form)))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                  #{}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                  (mapcat walk-symbols form))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    (vector? form) (mapcat walk-symbols form)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    (map? form) (mapcat walk-symbols (concat (keys form) (vals form)))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    (set? form) (mapcat walk-symbols form)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    (symbol? form) (if (namespace form) #{} #{form})\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    :else #{}))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n(defn- destructuring?\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  [binding]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  (not (symbol? binding)))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n(def ^:private kernel-gate-corpus\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  (edn/read-string (slurp (io/resource \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"yang/latte_oracle/kernel_gate.edn\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"))))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n(defn- kernel-symbol [{:keys [ns name]}]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  (symbol (str/replace (str ns) \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"_\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"-\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\") (str name)))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n(defn- kernel-guest-name [s]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  (symbol (str \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"gate-\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" (last (str/split (namespace s) #\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")) \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"-\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" (name s))))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n(defn- kernel-arities [form]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  (when (#{'defn 'defn-} (first form))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    (let [header (drop-while #(not (or (vector? %) (seq? %))) (nnext form))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n          params (if (vector? (first header)) [(first header)] (map first header))]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n      (mapv (fn [p] (if (some #{'&} p) [:variadic (.indexOf p '&)] (count p))) params))))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n(def ^:private kernel-entries\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  (mapv (fn [entry]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n          (let [s (kernel-symbol entry)]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n            (upstream-fn s) ; load the real aliases and refers before resolving source\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n            (assoc entry :symbol s :arities (kernel-arities (get top-forms [(:ns entry) (:name entry)])))))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n        manifest))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n(defn- kernel-resolve [ns-sym s]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  (when (symbol? s)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    (let [n (the-ns (symbol (str/replace (str ns-sym) \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"_\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"-\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n          v (ns-resolve n s)]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n      (when (and (var? v) (str/starts-with? (str (:ns (meta v))) \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"latte-kernel.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n        (symbol (str (:ns (meta v))) (str (:name (meta v))))))))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n(defn- kernel-rewrite\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Resolve library names against their actual upstream namespace, respecting\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   lexical binders and quote. No blanket alias stripping or data rewriting.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  [ns-sym form]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  (letfn [(bindings [pattern] (set (filter symbol? (tree-seq coll? seq pattern))))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n          (forms [xs bound] (map #(step % bound) xs))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n          (arity [xs bound]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n            (let [[params & body] xs]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n              (list* params (forms body (into bound (bindings params))))))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n          (step [x bound]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n            (cond\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n              (symbol? x) (cond\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                            (contains? bound x) x\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                            (#{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"set\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"clojure.set\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"} (namespace x)) (symbol (name x))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                            (= \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"pp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" (namespace x)) (symbol \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"clojure.pprint\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" (name x))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                            (contains? '{get-in lookup-in not-empty context-not-empty\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                                         ffirst context-ffirst list* context-list-star} x)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                            (get '{get-in lookup-in not-empty context-not-empty\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                                   ffirst context-ffirst list* context-list-star} x)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                            :else (if-let [s (kernel-resolve ns-sym x)]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                                    ;; empty-env at the immutable-context boundary\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                                    ;; is the same explicit initialization used by\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                                    ;; the slice-8 fixtures, including default arities.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                                    (if (= s 'latte-kernel.defenv/empty-env)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                                      initial-context\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                                      (if (and (= \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"latte-kernel.defenv\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" (namespace s))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                                               (str/starts-with? (name s) \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"->\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                                        (symbol (name s)) (kernel-guest-name s))) x))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n              (seq? x)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n              (let [[op & xs] x]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                (cond\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                  (= op 'quote) x\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                  (and (= op 'lazy-seq) (= ns-sym 'latte_kernel.utils) (= 'zip (second form)))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                  (step (second x) bound)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                  (#{'fn 'fn*} op)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                  (cons 'fn (if (vector? (first xs)) (arity xs bound)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                                (map #(arity % bound) xs)))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                  (#{'let 'loop} op)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                  (let [[bs & body] xs\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                        [bs' scope] (reduce (fn [[out scope] [p init]]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                                              [(conj out p (step init scope)) (into scope (bindings p))])\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                                            [[] bound] (partition 2 bs))]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                    (list* op bs' (forms body scope)))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                  ;; The slice-8 delta boundary: both namespaces use one binding.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                  (and (#{'deref 'clojure.core/deref} op) (= xs '(+unfold-implicit+)))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                  '(:unfold-implicit def-env)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                  :else (apply list (forms x bound))))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n              (vector? x) (mapv #(step % bound) x)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n              (map? x) (into (empty x) (map (fn [[k v]] [(step k bound) (step v bound)])) x)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n              (set? x) (into #{} (forms x bound))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n              :else x))]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    (let [[kind fname & header] form\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n          header (drop-while #(not (or (vector? %) (seq? %))) header)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n          guest (kernel-guest-name (kernel-symbol {:ns ns-sym :name fname}))]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n      (if (#{'defn 'defn-} kind)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n        (list* 'defn guest\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n               (if (vector? (first header)) (arity header #{}) (map #(arity % #{}) header)))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n        (list 'def guest (step (nth form 2) #{}))))))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n(def ^:private kernel-context-adapters\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  ;; Reuse the established slice-8 representation boundary; no new compiler\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  ;; workaround or truncated proof-step dispatcher is admitted here.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  '#{definition? theorem? axiom? notation? implicit? latte-definition?\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     local-definitions register-definition fetch-definition registered-definition? qualify-def})\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n(defn- kernel-source [{:keys [ns name symbol arities]}]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  (cond\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    (and (= ns 'latte_kernel.defenv) (contains? kernel-context-adapters name))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    (list* 'defn (kernel-guest-name symbol)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n           (map (fn [n]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                  (let [ps (mapv #(clojure.core/symbol (str \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"p\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" %)) (range n))]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                    (list ps (list* name ps)))) arities))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    :else (kernel-rewrite ns (get top-forms [ns name]))))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n(def ^:private kernel-sources\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  (into {} (map (fn [entry] [(kernel-guest-name (:symbol entry)) (kernel-source entry)])) kernel-entries))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n(defn- kernel-call [form]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  ;; Fixture code uses fully qualified names. Constructor adapters are the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  ;; five existing context constructors, outside the 143-binding manifest.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  (letfn [(rewrite [x]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n            (cond\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n              (and (seq? x) (= 'quote (first x))) x\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n              (symbol? x) (if (and (namespace x) (str/starts-with? (namespace x) \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"latte-kernel.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                            (if (str/starts-with? (name x) \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"->\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\") (symbol (name x)) (kernel-guest-name x)) x)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n              (seq? x) (apply list (map rewrite x))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n              (vector? x) (mapv rewrite x)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n              (map? x) (into {} (map (fn [[k v]] [(rewrite k) (rewrite v)])) x)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n              (set? x) (set (map rewrite x))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n              :else x))]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    (rewrite form)))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n(defn- kernel-closure [call]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  (let [sources (merge (into {} (map (juxt second identity)) context-forms) kernel-sources)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n        mentions #(filter (set (keys sources)) (walk-symbols %))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n        needed (loop [todo (seq (mentions call)) seen #{}]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                 (if-let [n (first todo)]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                   (if (contains? seen n) (recur (next todo) seen)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                       (recur (concat (next todo) (mentions (get sources n))) (conj seen n))) seen))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n        ordered (concat context-forms (map #(get kernel-sources (kernel-guest-name (:symbol %))) kernel-entries))]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    (filterv #(contains? needed (second %)) ordered)))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n(defn- kernel-fixture-call [{:keys [call definitions project-proof?]} guest?]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  (let [env (if guest? initial-context 'latte-kernel.defenv/empty-env)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n        register (if guest? 'register-definition 'latte-kernel.defenv/register-definition)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n        env (reduce (fn [env definition] (list register env (if guest? (kernel-call definition) definition))) env definitions)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n        call (if guest? (kernel-call call) call)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n        call (if project-proof?\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n               (list 'let ['r call] '(if (= :ok (first r)) [:ok (rest (second r))] r)) call)]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    (list 'let ['env env] call)))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n(defn- evidence-data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"EDN evidence retains all portable values and metadata. Nonportable host\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   payloads are explicit evidence, not accepted representation differences.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  [x]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  (cond\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    (fn? x) {:nonportable-host-value (str (class x))}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    (record? x) (evidence-data (upstream-record-data x))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    (map? x) (into {} (map (fn [[k v]] [(evidence-data k) (evidence-data v)])) x)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    (vector? x) (mapv evidence-data x)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    (set? x) (set (map evidence-data x))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    (seq? x) (apply list (map evidence-data x))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    :else x))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n(defn- kernel-attempt [f]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  (try (f)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n       (catch Exception e\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n         {:status :blocked :message (ex-message e) :data (evidence-data (ex-data e))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n          :causes (mapv (fn [cause] {:class (str (class cause)) :message (ex-message cause)})\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                        (take-while some? (iterate ex-cause e)))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n          :exception (str (class e))})))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n(defn- kernel-a [fixture]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  (kernel-attempt\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    #(let [value (if (= :unparser (:mode fixture))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                   (with-redefs-fn {(upstream-fn 'latte-kernel.unparser/+unparser-registry+)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                                   (atom {:fundamental [] :standard [] :user [] :unparsers {}})}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                     (fn []\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                       ((upstream-fn 'latte-kernel.unparser/register-unparser!) :gate (eval (:extension fixture)))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                       (a-leg (upstream-fn 'latte-kernel.unparser/unparse) [(:term fixture)])))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                   (a-leg (eval (list 'fn [] (kernel-fixture-call fixture false))) []))]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n       {:status :completed :outcome (evidence-data value) :shape (result-shape (evidence-data value))})))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n(defn- kernel-c-program [fixture]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  (if (= :unparser (:mode fixture))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    (list 'unparse (list 'register-unparser initial-context :gate (:extension fixture)) (list 'quote (:term fixture)))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    (kernel-fixture-call fixture true)))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n(defn- kernel-b [fixture]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  (kernel-attempt\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    #(let [sandbox (create-ns (gensym \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"kernel-gate-b-\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n           call (kernel-c-program fixture)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n           forms (kernel-closure call)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n           host-form (fn [form]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                       ;; Preserve the actual one-argument gensym call. Only\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                       ;; the slice-8 explicit two-argument supply is adapted.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                       (walk/postwalk\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                         (fn [x]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                           (if (and (seq? x) (= 'gensym (first x)) (= 2 (count x)))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                             (cons 'clojure.core/gensym (rest x)) x)) form))]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n       (try\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n         (binding [*ns* sandbox]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n           (refer 'clojure.core)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n           (require '[clojure.set :refer [union difference]])\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n           (eval (list* 'declare\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                        (concat (map second forms)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                                (for [[ns-sym source] all-forms\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                                      form source :when (= 'declare (first form))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                                      s (rest form)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                                      :let [qualified (kernel-resolve ns-sym s)]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                                      :when qualified]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                                  (kernel-guest-name qualified)))))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n           (doseq [form forms] (eval (context-host-form (host-form form))))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n           (let [v (a-leg (eval (list 'fn [] (context-host-form (host-form call)))) [])]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n             {:status :completed :outcome (evidence-data v) :shape (result-shape (evidence-data v))}))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n         (finally (remove-ns (ns-name sandbox)))))))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n(defn- kernel-compile [fixture]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  (let [call (kernel-c-program fixture)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n        forms (kernel-closure call)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n        program (conj forms call)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n        program (into (yang/library-for program) program)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n        ast (yang/compile-program program true arg-vector-opts)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n        missing (unbound-ast-symbols ast program)]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    (if (seq missing)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n      {:status :blocked :phase :admission :blocked-by (vec (sort missing))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n       :owners (into {} (for [s missing]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                         [s (mapv second (filter #(some #{s} (tree-seq coll? seq %)) program))]))}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n      {:status :compiled :ast ast :forms forms})))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n(defn- kernel-c [compiled lane]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  (if (= :compiled (:status compiled))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    (assoc (kernel-attempt\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n             #(let [v (compiler-test/run-guest-ast (:ast compiled) (oracle-registry yang/kind-module) lane 1000000)]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                {:status :completed :outcome (evidence-data v) :shape (result-shape (evidence-data v))}))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n           :lane lane)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    (assoc compiled :lane lane)))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n(defn- kernel-row [fixture]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  (let [a (kernel-a fixture)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n        b (kernel-b fixture)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n        compiled (kernel-attempt #(kernel-compile fixture))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n        compiled (if (and (= :blocked (:status compiled)) (not (:blocked-by compiled)))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                   (assoc compiled :phase :compile\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                          :blocked-by (if-let [n (get-in compiled [:data :name])] [n] [:compiler-exception])\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                          :minimal-source (get kernel-sources (get-in compiled [:data :name]))) compiled)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n        walker (kernel-c compiled :walker)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n        semantic (kernel-c compiled :semantic)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n        match? (and (= :completed (:status a) (:status b) (:status walker) (:status semantic))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                    (= (:outcome a) (:outcome b))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                    (agrees? (get a :outcome) (get walker :outcome))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                    (= (:outcome walker) (:outcome semantic))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                    (= (result-shape (:outcome a)) (result-shape (:outcome b)))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                    (if (contains? (:outcome a) :value)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                      (= (result-shape (:value (:outcome a)))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                         (result-shape (second (:outcome walker))))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                      (= (result-shape (get-in a [:outcome :thrown :data]))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                         (result-shape (get-in walker [:outcome 1 :yin.k/data])))))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n        status (cond match? :pass\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                     (some #(= :blocked (:status %)) [a b walker semantic]) :blocked\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                     :else :mismatch)]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    {:id (:id fixture) :negative? (boolean (:negative? fixture)) :status status\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     :dependency-of (:dependency-of fixture)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     :call (or (:call fixture) (kernel-c-program fixture))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     :a a :b b :c-walker walker :c-semantic semantic\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     :included-functions (mapv second (kernel-closure (kernel-c-program fixture)))}))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n(defn kernel-gate-evidence\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Run every fixture in A and independently in both C lanes. Compilation or\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   VM errors are blockers, never successful LaTTe rejections. Source closure\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   membership is recorded separately from conservative execution coverage.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  []\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  (let [results (mapv kernel-row (:fixtures kernel-gate-corpus))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n        inventory (mapv #(select-keys % [:symbol :kind :arities]) kernel-entries)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n        ;; Direct calls are a lower bound, not a claim that every function in\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n        ;; a dependency closure was executed. Unproven transitive arities stay\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n        ;; unexercised and block closure of the gate.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n        direct (into #{}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                     (for [[fixture row] (map vector (:fixtures kernel-gate-corpus) results)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                           :when (= :pass (:status row))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                           :let [call (:call fixture)]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                           :when (and (seq? call) (namespace (first call)))]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                       [(first call) (count (rest call))]))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n        all-arities (set (for [{:keys [symbol arities]} inventory n arities] [symbol n]))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n        unexercised (vec (sort-by pr-str (remove direct all-arities)))]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    {:slice 9 :gate-status (if (and (every? #(= :pass (:status %)) results) (empty? unexercised)) :pass :blocked)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     :generated-at (str (java.time.Instant/now))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     :adaptation-version {:context 1 :kernel-assembly 1}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     :executions {:a :original-upstream-clojure :b :context-source-clojure\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                  :c [:walker :semantic]}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     :upstream-revision \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"86fca0d1d054af005cb37395eae04500d45e6279\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     :compiler-vm-revision \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"f74f2cecccfc54813671555b15e39d254debd2d9\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     :runtime {:clojure (clojure-version) :java (System/getProperty \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"java.version\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     :instruction-budget-per-lane 1000000\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     :manifest-bindings (count manifest) :function-arity-candidates (count all-arities)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     :manifest-functions (count (filter :arities kernel-entries))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     :admitted-function-arity-count :not-recorded-in-inherited-manifest\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     :admission-note \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"The inherited manifest has no admitted/excluded dispositions or arities. All function arities are conservatively retained as gate obligations; no narrowing by fixture success.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     :coverage {:proven-direct-function-arities (vec (sort-by pr-str direct))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                :exercised-count (count direct) :unexercised unexercised\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                :transitive-execution-coverage :unproven\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                :inventory inventory}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     :counts (frequencies (map :status results)) :fixture-count (count results)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     :negative-fixture-count (count (filter :negative? results))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     :dependency-graph\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     (into (sorted-map)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n           (for [[fname source] kernel-sources]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n             [fname (vec (sort (filter (set (keys kernel-sources)) (walk-symbols source))))]))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     :fixtures results}))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n(defn write-kernel-gate-evidence!\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Explicit evidence refresh; normal test runs never update the checked-in oracle.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  []\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  (let [evidence (kernel-gate-evidence)]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    (with-open [w (io/writer \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_evidence.edn\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n      ;; prn keeps (quote ...) in valid EDN rather than pprint's reader\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n      ;; shorthand. One fixture per line keeps refreshes independently diffable.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n      (binding [*out* w *print-length* nil *print-level* nil]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n        (print \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n        (doseq [[k v] (dissoc evidence :fixtures)] (pr k) (print \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\") (prn v))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n        (println \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":fixtures [\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n        (doseq [row (:fixtures evidence)] (prn row))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n        (println \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    (select-keys evidence [:gate-status :counts :fixture-count :manifest-bindings :function-arity-candidates :coverage])))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n(deftest test-kernel-differential-gate\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  (let [evidence (kernel-gate-evidence)]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    (is (= (count (:fixtures kernel-gate-corpus)) (count (set (map :id (:fixtures evidence)))))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Every named fixture runs exactly once, including negatives\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    (doseq [row (:fixtures evidence)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n            :when (and (:negative? row) (= :completed (get-in row [:a :status])))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n            :let [outcome (get-in row [:a :outcome]) value (:value outcome)]]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n      (is (or (:thrown outcome) (false? value) (and (sequential? value) (= :ko (first value))))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n          (str \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"A must actually reject the named negative: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" (:id row))))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    (println \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"KERNEL-GATE\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" (pr-str (select-keys evidence [:gate-status :counts :fixture-count :manifest-bindings :function-arity-candidates])))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    (doseq [row (:fixtures evidence) :when (not= :pass (:status row))]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n      (println \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"KERNEL-BLOCKER\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n               (pr-str {:id (:id row) :status (:status row)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                        :blocked-by (get-in row [:c-walker :blocked-by])\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                        :a (get-in row [:a :status]) :b (get-in row [:b :status])\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                        :c-walker (get-in row [:c-walker :status])\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                        :c-semantic (get-in row [:c-semantic :status])})))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    (is (= :pass (:gate-status evidence))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n        (str \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Kernel gate remains blocked: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" (:counts evidence)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n             \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"; admitted/candidate but unexercised function/arities=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" (count (get-in evidence [:coverage :unexercised]))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n             \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\". See slice9_evidence.edn; blocked fixtures are not accepted negatives.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"))))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n;; Regenerate the LaTTe oracle's derived tables from the manifest forms:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n;;   test/yang/latte_oracle/throw_sites.edn  (the throw-site inventory)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n;;   test/yang/latte_oracle/case_arms.edn    (the per-arm case fixtures)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n;; Both are derived by yang.latte-oracle-test, so this script and the test\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n;; cannot disagree about what a regenerated table holds.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n;; Run: clj -X:test:dev latte-oracle-tables/-main\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n(ns latte-oracle-tables\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  (:require [clojure.java.io :as io]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n            [clojure.pprint :as pp]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n            [yang.latte-oracle-test]))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n(defn- derived\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"The result of calling the oracle test's private derivation `sym`.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  [sym]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  ((deref (ns-resolve 'yang.latte-oracle-test sym))))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n(defn- write-table!\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  [file header rows]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  (io/make-parents file)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  (spit file (str header (with-out-str (pp/pprint rows))))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  (println \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"wrote\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" (count rows) \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"rows to\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" file))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n(defn -main\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  [& _]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  (write-table! \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"test/yang/latte_oracle/throw_sites.edn\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                (str \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\";; GENERATED from the manifest forms by yang.latte-oracle-test/throw-site-rows.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                     \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\";; One row per throw symbol; disposition :fixture | :deferred | :excluded.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                (derived 'throw-site-rows))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  (write-table! \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"test/yang/latte_oracle/case_arms.edn\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                (str \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\";; GENERATED from the manifest forms by yang.latte-oracle-test/case-arm-rows.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                     \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\";; One row per case site: each arm's clause constants, and whether it has a default.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                (derived 'case-arm-rows))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  (shutdown-agents))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n# Slice 9 kernel differential gate \\\\u2014 BLOCKED\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThis is a failing close-out gate, not a conformance certificate. No compiler or\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nVM source was changed. No commit was made.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe 54 fixtures in `kernel_gate.edn` invoke actual pinned upstream functions on A,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nexecute the explicit context source on host Clojure on B, and compile the guest\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nsource for C-walker and C-semantic. Guest extension closures are evaluated by the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nVM; the harness supplies no host callback primitive. The original proof dispatcher\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nis assembled, rather than substituting slice 8's restricted state-step dispatcher.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nEvery fixture, including every negative, has an A/B/C-walker/C-semantic outcome in\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n`slice9_evidence.edn`. Blocked fixtures are attempted and recorded independently;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nno negative is skipped or counted as a successful guest rejection.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nResult: **4 passing fixtures, 2 mismatches, 48 blocked fixtures**. Passing fixtures\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nare `:subst-capture`, `:subst-shadow`, `:subst-three-arity`, and\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n`:unparser-guest-closure`. The compile/admission blockers occur before either C\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nlane executes those blocked programs; both lane records explicitly say so.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n## Mismatches with minimal repros\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n1. `:minimal-gensym-freshness`:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   ```clojure\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   (let [a (gensym \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"fresh\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\") b (gensym \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"fresh\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")] (= a b))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   ```\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   A and B return `false`; both C lanes return `[:yin.k/ok true]`. The guest\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   library's one-argument `gensym` constructs `G__fresh` repeatedly. This\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   dependency is reachable from `latte-kernel.typing/rebuild-type`. No fresh-name\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   correspondence can turn equality of two names into inequality.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n2. `:free-vars-local-capture`:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   ```clojure\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   (latte-kernel.syntax/free-vars\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     (latte-kernel.defenv/register-definition env\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n       (latte-kernel.defenv/->Definition 'd [] 0 'x '#{x} 'A {}) true)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     '(d))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   ```\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   A returns `#{x}`; B returns `#{}`; both C lanes return `[:yin.k/ok #{}]`.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   The upstream `free-vars` implementation uses `(second def-env)` to access\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   local definitions. The inherited context adaptation passes a context map in\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   that position. This is an A/B adaptation mismatch, independently of compilation.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n## Blocked dependencies\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Parsing reaches `butlast`, `last`, bare `nth`, and `kind/var?`, which are not\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  admitted by the supplied portable modules. Minimal independent fixtures for\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  `last`, `nth`, and `var?` are included. The parser's valid and malformed cases\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  all run on A/B, but their guest dependency closures fail admission.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Normalization reaches `last` in `nbe/evaluation` and `with-meta` in\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  `nbe/quotation-`. `:minimal-last` and `:minimal-with-meta` isolate these failures.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  Beta, transparent delta, opaque delta, and each required public normalization\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  arity have named fixtures; no host normalization is substituted for C.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Typing reaches the actual `typing/unfold-implicit` `try/catch`, including\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  `.getMessage`, `ex-data`, and exception bindings. Slice 8's already-typed\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  extension adapter does not replace this full typed-argument path. The two\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  implicit fixtures use actual guest closure source and remain blocked.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- `typing/type-of-ascribe` is declared but has no definition in the pinned\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  upstream source and no manifest entry. `:typing-ascription` also exposes the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  upstream unbound-function failure on A. It is never treated as a successful\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  type rejection by C.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Full proof elaboration/checking reaches `proof/+opacity-fn+`, an ambient atom\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  initialized with a closure. Yang rejects this `def` initializer under the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  outcome convention. Each affected fixture records\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  `:blocked-by [gate-proof-+opacity-fn+]` and the exact `:minimal-source`.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  The inherited partial proof-step context adapter cannot stand in for the real\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  parsing/typing dispatcher. Proof compilation separately reaches the missing\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  `string?` dependency; even `:compile-proof`'s single `:qed` script is explicitly\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  blocked by this dependency rather than treated as a successful rejection.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Upstream's error for steps after `qed` includes the host `clojure.core/meta`\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  function in its `:meta` field. Evidence explicitly marks this nonportable host\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  value; it is not normalized into an accepted portability difference. The\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  malformed scalar proof-step fixture also records its native upstream exception.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe complete source dependency graph, per-fixture closure membership, missing\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nsymbols and their owning definitions, compiler exception causes, and minimal\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ncalls are retained in `slice9_evidence.edn`. Compiler/admission/VM exceptions are\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nblockers; only actual returned `:ko`, `false`, or corresponding domain exceptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ncan satisfy negative fixtures. A test assertion checks that every completed A\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nnegative really rejects its input.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n## Manifest and coverage\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe inherited manifest contains **155 bindings, 147 functions, and 175\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nfunction/arity entries**,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nnot the plan's earlier estimate of 143 definitions. It has no admitted/excluded\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ndispositions, and its source fields are nil. Consequently an exact admitted\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nfunction/arity denominator cannot be recovered honestly from that manifest.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n`admitted-function-arity-count` is explicitly `:not-recorded-in-inherited-manifest`.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nAll 175 entries are retained as gate obligations; successful fixtures do not\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nnarrow the denominator.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe conservative, proven direct A/B/C agreement count is **2/175 arities**:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n`latte-kernel.syntax/subst` at arities 2 and 3. The successful unparser integration\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nalso executes its dependencies, but this harness does not claim an exact dynamic\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ntransitive arity count. It records `:transitive-execution-coverage :unproven`.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nAll **173 remaining unexercised-or-unproven entries** are individually listed\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nunder `:coverage :unexercised`, alongside the complete function/arity inventory.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nDependency closure membership is recorded separately and does not count as\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nexecution. This incomplete accounting itself blocks the close-out gate.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n## Reproduction and verification\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nPins: upstream LaTTe `86fca0d1d054af005cb37395eae04500d45e6279`; compiler/VM\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n`f74f2cecccfc54813671555b15e39d254debd2d9`; context adaptation v1, kernel assembly v1.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe recorded host uses Clojure 1.12.4 and Java 17.0.18. Each C execution has a\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n1,000,000-instruction budget. There is no continuation-depth claim for blocked\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nprograms.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nRun the gate:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```sh\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nclj -M:test -n yang.latte-oracle-test\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**22 tests, 988 assertions, 1 failure, 0 errors, exit 1.** The single failed\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nassertion is `test-kernel-differential-gate`: the gate must remain red while the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nabove blockers or unproven coverage remain. The inherited 21 tests passed in the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nbaseline: 968 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors. Do not remove the close-out\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nassertion to manufacture the requested zero-failure result.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nExplicitly refresh evidence from fresh A/B/C runs (normal test runs do not rewrite\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nit):\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```sh\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nclj -Sdeps '{:aliases {:gate {:main-opts [\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"-e\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"(require (quote yang.latte-oracle-test)) (println (select-keys (yang.latte-oracle-test/write-kernel-gate-evidence!) [:gate-status :counts :fixture-count :manifest-bindings :function-arity-candidates]))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]}}}' -M:test:gate\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThis evidence-writing command returns normally even when the recorded gate is\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nblocked; only the test command above is the acceptance gate.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nUnchanged regression suites:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```sh\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nclj -M:test -n yang.clojure-test -n yin.vm.macro-test -n yang.clojure.stream-eval-test -n yin.vm.store-write-audit-test\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Blocked at namespace loading**, `ClassNotFoundException:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nyang.python.antlr.gen.Python3Lexer`; no green four-suite result. The stream/REPL\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nsuite imports the frontend catalog that requires the generated Python parser.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe prerequisite attempt\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n`clj -M:antlr-gen --grammar python3 --target java` failed with\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n`java.nio.channels.UnresolvedAddressException` while retrieving required inputs.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe independent suites were then run separately:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```sh\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nclj -M:test -n yang.clojure-test -n yin.vm.macro-test -n yin.vm.store-write-audit-test\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nclj -M:test -n yin.vm.semantic.linearize-test -n yin.vm.semantic.analysis-test -n yin.vm.semantic.frame-test\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nRespectively **106 tests / 1,007 assertions** and **45 tests / 1,944 assertions**,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nboth with **0 failures and 0 errors**.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\