d**.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nEvery fixture has independent A, B, C-walker and C-semantic records in\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n[\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'`slice9_evidence.edn`](slice9_evidence.edn). Each passing row additionally\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nrecords explicit A/B, A/C-walker, A/C-semantic and C/C agreement flags. No host\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nparser, normalizer, type checker, proof dispatcher or extension callback replaces\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nguest execution. The assume/have/discharge proof passes within the unchanged\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n1,000,000-instruction limit on both C lanes.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n## Admission denominator\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe regenerated manifest contains 155 bindings: **146 admitted, 9 excluded**.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nIts 147 functions have 175 candidate function/arity entries: **165 admitted,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n10 excluded**. Exclusions name clock access, host pprint/output capture, and\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nfunctions that directly use those diagnostics. Their guest entry points raise\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nan explicit nonportable-binding refusal if reached; excluding a diagnostic\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nbinding does not exclude the proof dispatcher that contains a diagnostic arm.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe proven direct A/B/C execution count is **22/165 admitted arities**. The\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nremaining **143** admitted entries are individually listed under\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n`:coverage :unexercised`. Transitive execution coverage remains **unproven**;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nsource dependency membership never substitutes for execution. Fixture success\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ndoes not narrow the admission denominator. These obligations independently keep\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nthe final gate open.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nRegenerate admission decisions and the existing derived throw/case tables with:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```sh\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nclj -X:test:dev latte-oracle-tables/-main\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n## Closed dependencies and explicit conventions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Guest implementations admit `butlast`, `last`, bare `nth`, `string?`, `update`,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  and callable collections; the compiler lowers `->` through ordinary control\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  forms. Callable collections use the guest library, with ordinary closures\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  taking the direct callable path.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- `kind/var?` explicitly admits the JVM Clojure Var predicate. Namespace lookup\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  still requires a separately installed host capability.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Metadata attachment uses a declared pure **`kind/with-meta` seam**. This is a\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  departure from the requested guest-only implementation: metadata is carried\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  on existing host symbols/collections, and the current `data` module exposes\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  no operation that can attach it. Introducing a second tagged representation\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  would change symbol identity and every collection boundary. No Yin source or\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  ABI was changed; domain metadata is checked by the existing shape comparison.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Fresh allocation consumes immutable `{:counter N}` data and returns\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  `[symbol next-supply]`, constructing `G__<prefix><N>`. The original A call\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  `(let [a (gensym \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"fresh\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\") b (gensym \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"fresh\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")] (= a b))` returns false.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  B/C thread the supply explicitly through the corresponding two allocations,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  also returning false. Prefix-only ambient allocation is refused; no hidden\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  mutable counter is installed. Numeric deterministic constructors remain\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  compatible with slice 8. `rebuild-type` returns `[original-result next-context]`,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  and its proof caller binds that next context explicitly.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- The free-vars argument boundary extracts the original global/local definition\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  pair from `:definitions` before entering the upstream body. Its original\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  `(second def-env)` access is preserved; local capture now returns `#{x}` on A,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  B and both C lanes.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- The actual `typing/unfold-implicit` source runs through portable `try/catch`.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  Throws retain early-return outcomes; exception bindings carry error data;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  `.getMessage`, `ex-message`, and `ex-data` access that data. Both the typed and\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  throwing guest extension fixtures pass. Unsupported host accessors such as\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  `.getStackTrace` are refused at compile time and recorded in the evidence.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- The former opacity atom names the explicit `:opacity-policy` context field.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  Installation returns an updated context. The real upstream proof dispatcher\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  threads that context through opaque/transparent arms; the two added opacity\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  fixtures pass without substituting slice 8'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'s restricted dispatcher.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nObserver exceptions can attach an entire host VM session. Evidence records\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nwhether that diagnostic snapshot was attached and retains its exception data\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nand causes, without recursively expanding the VM's duplicated closure\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n environments. It does not remove domain error payloads.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n## Remaining mismatches with minimal repros\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nBoth mismatches arise from upstream placing the **host \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'`clojure.core/meta`\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nfunction itself** in after-qed error data. A and B retain that nonportable host\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nvalue; C carries its guest closure. This difference is not accepted or erased.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```clojure\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n;; :elab-after-qed\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n(latte-kernel.proof/elab-proof env []\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'[[:qed (lambda [A :type] (lambda [x A] x)) {}]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    [:qed missing {}]])\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n;; :check-after-qed\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n(latte-kernel.proof/check-proof env [] 'late '\\\\u2733\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  '[[:qed (lambda [A :type] (lambda [x A] x)) {}]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    [:qed missing {}]])\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'```\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe two remaining blockers are upstream failures, not accepted negative results:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```clojure\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n;; :typing-ascription \\\\u2014 pinned upstream declares type-of-ascribe but never\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n;; defines it. A raises an unbound-function error; B/C refuse that exact branch.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n(latte-kernel.typing/type-of-term env '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'[[A \\\\u2733] [x A]]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  '(:latte-kernel.syntax/ascribe x A))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n;; :compile-malformed \\\\u2014 A and B raise native scalar-sequence exceptions.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n;; C returns a portable sequence refusal, which is not counted as agreement.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n(latte-kernel.proof/compile-proof '[42])\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'```\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n## Verification\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe required compiler, macro, stream-eval and store-write-audit regression suites\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\npass: **122 tests, 1,337 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n```sh\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nclj -M:test -n yang.clojure-test -n yin.vm.macro-test '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  -n yang.clojure.stream-eval-test -n yin.vm.store-write-audit-test\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nclj -M:test -n yang.latte-oracle-test\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'```\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe oracle suite retains exactly the expected close-out gate failure; the other\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\noracle tests pass. The manifest schema and gate assertions check dispositions,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nthe admitted/excluded partition, unique fixture execution, negative outcomes,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nand agreement records. Clj-kondo reports **0 errors, 2 inherited warnings, no new\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nwarnings**. Cljstyle and `git diff --check` pass.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe stream suite'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'s generated-parser prerequisites were rebuilt locally from\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ncopied immutable cached inputs, with the repository generator checking all\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\npinned input and generated-source digests. No other checkout's mutable build\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\noutputs are shared. The acceptance above executes both C evaluators on the JVM;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nit does not claim a new Node or Dart host verification run.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe pinned upstream revision is \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'`86fca0d1d054af005cb37395eae04500d45e6279`.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe evidence records the base compiler/VM revision, exact compiler source SHA-256,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nhost versions, context/assembly adaptation version 2, unchanged instruction\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nbudget, admission inventory, and dependency graph. Normal tests do not rewrite\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nchecked-in evidence; explicit refresh uses\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n`yang.latte-oracle-test/write-kernel-gate-evidence!`.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nMD\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\npython3 - <<'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'PY'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\np='test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_gate.md';s=open(p).read().replace('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n environments.', '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nenvironments.');open(p,'w').write(s)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nPY\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":null,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"in_progress\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ncollab/1793294621496-compiler-engineer-hardening2.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log:183:{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"item.completed\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"item_95\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"tail -8 /tmp/h2-oracl