\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Kernel gate remains blocked: {:pass 53, :blocked 2, :mismatch 2}; admitted/candidate but unexercised function/arities=143. See slice9_evidence.edn; blocked fixtures are not accepted negatives.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nexpected: (= :pass (:gate-status evidence))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  actual: (not (= :pass :blocked))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nORACLE latte-kernel.defenv/mkenv A= [[] {}] C= {:status :ok, :value [[] {}]}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nORACLE latte-kernel.utils/vectorn? A= true C= {:status :ok, :value true}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nRan 23 tests containing 997 assertions.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n1 failures, 0 errors.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ncollab/1793294621496-compiler-engineer-hardening2.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log:209:{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"item.started\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"item_109\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"cat > /tmp/h2-commit-message.txt <<'TXT'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nfix(yang.clojure): close kernel hardening dependency blockers\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nRecord manifest admission dispositions and admit missing guest operations.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nLower portable try/catch and thread fresh-name and opacity contexts explicitly.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nRaise fixture agreement from 4/54 to 53/57 while retaining the blocked gate,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ntwo named mismatches, two upstream failures and unproven arity coverage.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nDocument the explicit-supply and metadata representation seams.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nValidation: 145 tests, 2335 assertions, zero errors and only the expected\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nclose-out gate failure. Regression suites pass; kondo has zero errors and\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nno new warnings.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nTXT\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n git diff --cached --check\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":null,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"in_progress\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ncollab/1793294621496-compiler-engineer-hardening2.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log:210:{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"item.completed\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"item_109\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"cat > /tmp/h2-commit-message.txt <<'TXT'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nfix(yang.clojure): close kernel hardening dependency blockers\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nRecord manifest admission dispositions and admit missing guest operations.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nLower portable try/catch and thread fresh-name and opacity contexts explicitly.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nRaise fixture agreement from 4/54 to 53/57 while retaining the blocked gate,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ntwo named mismatches, two upstream failures and unproven arity coverage.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nDocument the explicit-supply and metadata representation seams.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nValidation: 145 tests, 2335 assertions, zero errors and only the expected\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nclose-out gate failure. Regression suites pass; kondo has zero errors and\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nno new warnings.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nTXT\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n git diff --cached --check\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ncollab/1793296786225-reviewer-hardening2.glm-5.3.stdout.log:7:**Verdict: the round's claims are substantiated.** The 4\\\\u219250 pass improvement on the unchanged 54-fixture baseline is produced by real guest machinery, not loosened fixtures; the admission inventory is sound and conservatively defaults new bindings to admitted; the 143 unexercised arities are honest accounting that independently keeps the gate open. Four P3 findings below; no P0\\\\u2013P2. The requested judgment on the kind/`var?` + `with-meta` departure: **justified, with two carried obligations**.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ncollab/1793296786225-reviewer-hardening2.glm-5.3.stdout.log:11:**P3 | src/dev/latte_oracle_manifest.clj:50-57** | The stale manifest generator still rewrites `test/yang/latte_oracle/manifest.edn` in the old schema (no `:disposition`/`:admission-reason`), while `latte-oracle-tables/-main` (src/dev/latte_oracle_tables.clj:48-51) is now the writer of record. Running the old tool per its own docstring (`clj -M -m latte-oracle-manifest`) wipes the admission inventory from the working tree; the schema assertion in `test-oracle-classification` (test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:281-283) then fails loudly, but the checked-in inventory is lost and the old header comment is now false. | Fix: delete `latte-oracle-manifest` or reduce it to a delegation to `latte-oracle-tables`, and update its docstring.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ncollab/1793296786225-reviewer-hardening2.glm-5.3.stdout.log:13:**P3 | src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:895-919** | The portable `try` lowerer's catch arm fires on *any* `[error-tag v]`: it binds `(data/nth outcome 1)` (line ~912) without discriminating the thrown value. A thrown non-ex-info value (e.g. `(throw \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"boom\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")` inside `(try \\\\u2026 (catch Exception e \\\\u2026))`) is caught by the guest but propagates in Clojure (a thrown String is not an Exception). The catch-class guard (lines 903-905) constrains only the *syntax* of the clause, not the runtime class of the thrown value. Unexercised: all kernel sources throw ex-info only, and `test-portable-try-outcomes` (test/yang/clojure_test.clj:2024) tests ex-info throws exclusively. | Fix: either record the limitation in the library notes next to the other \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"known compromises\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" (clojure.cljc:1908-1916), or discriminate at runtime (catch only values carrying `:yin.k/message`, re-propagating others).\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ncollab/1793296786225-reviewer-hardening2.glm-5.3.stdout.log:15:**P3 | src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1163-1166** | Callable collections route through `invoke-value` only when the operator is a **local** or a **non-symbol** (`(or (contains? (locals env) operator) (not (symbol? operator)))`). A top-level defined collection \\\\u2014 `(def v [1 2]) (v 0)` \\\\u2014 compiles to a plain `:application` and errors at runtime instead of indexing, diverging from Clojure. Untested boundary of the \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"callable collections\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" admission (test/yang/clojure_test.clj:2049 uses only `let`-bound collections). | Fix: record as a known boundary in the library notes, or extend the route to operators in `::defined`.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ncollab/1793296786225-reviewer-hardening2.glm-5.3.stdout.log:17:**P3 | src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1918-1926** | `kind-arities` publishes `'var? [1]` unconditionally (line 1926) while `kind-module` provides `var?` only under `#?(:clj \\\\u2026 :default {})` (line 1920) \\\\u2014 on a Node/Dart host the arity profile would admit a binding the module cannot supply. Relatedly, metadata attached via the new `kind/with-meta` seam has no stated serialization-survival guarantee: no fixture round-trips a meta'd value through the store/encoder, so `meta` after restoration is unspecified. | Fix: gate the published arity with the same reader conditional (or register the capability per-host at harness setup), and add a note/obligation that host metadata is not a serialized ABI field.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ncollab/1793296786225-reviewer-hardening2.glm-5.3.stdout.log:37:7. **143 unexercised arities.** Honest: `direct` counts only `:pass` rows' original calls (latte_oracle_test.clj:1746-1752); the denominator is the disposition inventory independent of fixture success; 165 \\\\u2212 22 = 143, each listed under `:coverage :unexercised`; the admitted+excluded partition of the 175 candidates is asserted (line 1831-1833). The only denominator shrinkage vs baseline is the 10 excluded arities \\\\u2014 the disclosed admission change itself. The close-out test deliberately asserts `:pass` against a `:blocked` reality, keeping the suite red until the gate truly closes.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ncollab/1793294621496-compiler-engineer-hardening2.prompt.md:15:- test/yang/latte_oracle/ (manifest admission dispositions + fixture additions)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ncollab/1793294621496-compiler-engineer-hardening2.prompt.md:23:1. MANIFEST ADMISSION DISPOSITIONS: the manifest (test/yang/latte_oracle/manifest.edn) records no admitted/excluded dispositions (the gate recorded :not-recorded-in-inherited-manifest). Extend the manifest schema and src/dev/latte_oracle_tables.clj so every binding carries :disposition :admitted | :excluded + :admission-reason, regenerate the table, and make the gate's coverage denominator read it. Admitted = reachable through the guest library + data module + admitted host seams (kind/*); excluded = genuinely nonportable (nano-time, pprint, host interop) with reasons. The gate-report format gains an honest admitted-vs-excluded denominator.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ncollab/1793296786225-reviewer-hardening2.prompt.md:17:dispositions (schema + regeneration + denominator), stdlib admissions (butlast/last/nth/\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ncollab/1793296786225-reviewer-hardening2.prompt.md:30:(.getMessage/ex-data paths); the meta-host-value mismatch disposition (upstream deviation\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ncollab/1793296786225-reviewer-hardening2.prompt.md:38:Report findings as: P0-P3 | file:line | evidence | fix. State \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"No actionable findings\\\\\\\