{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"agent_message","text":"The JSON depth change is off by one: this tip returns `false` for `json_encode([1],0,1)`, but PHP 8.3.35 permits it and rejects `[[1]]` at that depth. The new regression pins the wrong result. Focused probes also show that `.1` and `1.` still decode successfully.\n\nAll six records have the requested provenance fields, but five pair a November 4 run date with `06cd429f`, a commit created November 6. I couldn’t access the named logs because this environment cannot resolve shiva. The seat gate is still running."}}
