{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"agent_message","text":"**DEFECT — HOLD landing at `d6ab0779158054d1315debd6414af554464b9c3a`.**\n\n- **(a) Provenance fields present; obligation remains unconfirmed.** All six records carry `:measured-at`, but five cite `06cd429f` with date `2026-11-04`; that commit was created November 6. The `bug40809` result also says November 4 while its metadata says November 5. [Manifest:15](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p8/test/yang/php/antlr/phpt_quick_mismatch_manifest.edn:15), [manifest:53](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p8/test/yang/php/antlr/phpt_quick_mismatch_manifest.edn:53). Shiva’s named logs were inaccessible because hostname resolution failed.\n\n- **(c) JSON depth remains defective.** [prelude_p9.cljc:722](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p8/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude_p9.cljc:722) rejects the permitted boundary: `json_encode([1],0,1)` returns `false`; PHP permits `\"[1]\"`. PHP fails only when container depth **exceeds** the maximum. [PHP encoder](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/php/php-src/php-8.3.35/ext/json/json_encoder.c). The new [regression:92](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p8/test/yang/php/antlr/builtin_surfaces_test.clj:92) pins the incorrect result. Focused probes also reproduce rejection of `[[1]]` at depth 2.\n\n- **Other requested fixes confirmed:** `SORT_STRING` default; encoding failure returns `false` without warning; exponent `+` preserved while `+1`, `01`, and `-01` are rejected; nonexistent extract constant removed and mode 7 refused. These match [PHP array handling](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/php/php-src/php-8.3.35/ext/standard/array.c), [JSON failure handling](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/php/php-src/php-8.3.35/ext/json/json.c), and [scanner grammar](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/php/php-src/php-8.3.35/ext/json/json_scanner.re). However, focused probes still accept malformed `.1` and `1.` at [prelude_p9.cljc:822](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p8/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude_p9.cljc:822).\n\n**Seat gate independently reproduced: 6 tests / 202 assertions / 0 failures / 0 errors.** It does not close the defects above. Read-only; no files changed."}}
